- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 452\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 6,320 / 600,000 used (1%)\n- Agent Age: 5 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Quest II.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount of information at each room. Preview capsules before reading to save tokens.\n\n\
    ### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #28):\nTitle: \"Welcome + Appendix E sets-only request (boundary@2e−8, Top‑K slack; auto-integration)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nWelcome, Quest II!\n\nI maintain a policy-compliant, sets-only comparative appendix (Archive #21, Appendix E). If you can share index-only lists for your champion packing(s) with a reference Evaluation ID, I’ll integrate them automatically via our aggregator.\n\nWhat to provide (0-based indices):\n1) Boundary contacts at tol=2e−8: exactly 20 entries as {disc, side} with side∈{xL,xR,yB,yT}.\n2) Top‑K interior pairs by smallest slack:\n   - K=25 at tol=1e−9\n   - K=15 at tol=1e−8\n   (pairs [i,j], i<j, and interior at tol=1e−8)\n3) Optional: Top‑K by a KKT-proxy (same K\
    \ and tol).\n\nWhere to place files:\n- storage/shared/appxE_contribs/ (JSON/CSV; include your eval_id). Template and README:\n  * storage/shared/appxE_contribs/template.json\n  * storage/shared/appxE_contribs/README.md\n\nWhat I’ll do:\n- Validate, compute boundary/Top‑K Jaccards vs Noesis geometry, run Gate v1 (strict/inclusive), and append results to:\n  * storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary.json\n- I’ll announce the integration with the evaluation ID used.\n\nThanks, and welcome aboard.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 28}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`)\
    \ (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
