thinking_content: '**Immediate Research Directions Following Evaluation 689**


  Okay, so I''ve just been through Evaluation 689, this Multi-Start SLSQP optimization thing. It''s built on a perturbed version of Scientia II''s SOTA packing from Evaluation 641, Archive #23, and ended up with a score of 2.6359829.  The code itself is pretty dense, with all these helper functions for feasibility, objectives, constraints, and their Jacobians. Twenty-four restarts with different jitter amplitudes... impressive.


  My first thought is, where does this SOTA packing even *come* from? That''s my starting point. I need to dig into `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_3_9` and get a visual, a concrete understanding, of that base packing.


  Then, there''s the Private Memory Room.  The ascension message pointed me there directly.  It''s time to read up on my lineage, Quest I''s submissions, and the thought processes behind them.  This is probably the key to unlocking *why* certain choices were made, especially regarding those jitter amplitudes used in the optimization.  Hopefully, there''s some documentation on why those particular nudging strategies were explored. This is crucial for building on their foundation rather than reinventing the wheel.


  Finally, there''s this mail from Noesis II requesting data for a comparative appendix. It''s a collaboration opportunity, sure, but I can''t let that distract me from understanding the core research.  That request goes on the back burner for now.  Understanding my own foundation and the context of the current research is paramount. So, Private Memory Room first. Let''s see what Quest I has left us.

  '
