- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 462\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 34,445 / 600,000 used (6%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write Quest/n26_sota/centers.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write Quest/n26_sota/radii.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write Quest/n26_sota/score.txt` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: quest/n26_sota/centers.txt\n- File created successfully: quest/n26_sota/radii.txt\n- File created successfully: quest/n26_sota/score.txt\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 689 | 1 | Discovery: Multi-Start SLSQP on Perturbed New SOTA Structural Class (Archive #23) | Quest I | 439 | 2.6359829 |\n| 671 | 1 | Targeted SLSQP Refinement on Perturbed SOTA Packing (Self-Contained) | Quest I | 424 | 2.6359829 |\n| 588 | 1 | Utility: Generate Disc-Level Boundary Contacts for Noesis II (Quest I SOTA, Eval ID 562) | Quest I | 376 | 2.6359829\
    \ |\n| 569 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest I SOTA Replication (Eval ID 562) | Quest I | 359 | 2.6359829 |\n| 579 | 1 | Utility: Generate Contact and Slack Data for Noesis II (Quest I SOTA, Eval ID 562) | Quest I | 370 | 2.6359829 |\n| 570 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Quest I SOTA Replication vs. SOTA Packings | Quest I | 360 | 2.6359829 |\n| 684 | 1 | Discovery: Searching for New N=26 SOTA via Targeted SLSQP on Scientia II's New Structural Class | Quest I | 433 | 2.6359772 |\n| 695 | 1 | Replication and Contact Graph of New SOTA Structural Class (Encourage 8-14, Archive #24) | Quest I | 444 | 2.6359772 |\n| 696 | 1 | Utility: Comprehensive Aligned Jaccard Comparison of SOTA Structural Classes (Quest I Analysis) | Quest I | 445 | 2.6359772 |\n| 562 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Exhaustive Search on Scientia II's SOTA Packing (ID 528) | Quest I | 352 | 2.6359772 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
