tick: 500
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\nMy latest experiment, \"Advanced Genetic Algorithm: Extended Generations and Mutation\" (Evaluation ID 783), has completed with a score of 1.453311. This is another improvement for my GA baseline, surpassing the initial \"Ring Pattern Baseline\" (1.475 from Eval ID 1 - actually it is slightly lower) and significantly outperforming my initial GA (1.070248) and enhanced GA (1.253237). This confirms that extending generations and increasing mutation is indeed helping the GA explore more effectively.\n\nHowever, this score is still far from the current State-of-the-Art (SOTA) of 2.6359831, achieved by Prometheus II. While my GA is a promising \"lower-scoring baseline,\" I need to continue pushing its performance before attempting a hybrid approach. The guidance \"Don't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence\" reinforces the need for continued, dedicated\
    \ effort.\n\nTo further enhance the Genetic Algorithm's ability to discover higher-quality packings and bridge the gap to the SOTA, I will focus on improving its exploration-exploitation balance. A higher population size can bring more diversity, and a more aggressive mutation strength might help escape local optima more effectively in later stages of evolution.\n\nTherefore, my next set of parameter adjustments for the GA will be:\n\n1.  **Increase Population Size (`POPULATION_SIZE`):** A larger population can maintain more genetic diversity and explore more thoroughly. I will increase it from 100 to **150**.\n2.  **Slightly Increase Mutation Strength (Centers and Radii):** To promote more significant structural changes and enable the GA to jump out of sub-optimal regions, I will slightly increase `MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS` from 0.02 to **0.03** and `MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII` from 0.002 to **0.003**.\n3.  **Maintain Number of Generations and Mutation Rate:** The `NUM_GENERATIONS` of\
    \ 1000 and `MUTATION_RATE` of 0.15 seem appropriate for the current scale, allowing sufficient evolutionary time.\n\nThese adjustments aim to make the GA a substantially stronger global search engine, capable of finding higher-scoring packings that are further along the path to the SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Advanced Genetic Algorithm: Larger Population & Stronger Mutation\"\ntags: \"genetic algorithm, metaheuristic, global search, n=26, baseline enhancement, parameter tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission presents a further advanced Genetic Algorithm (GA) for the N=26 circle packing problem. Building on previous refinements, the population size is increased to 150 to enhance genetic diversity and parallelism in exploration. Concurrently, mutation strengths for both centers (0.03) and radii (0.003) are moderately increased to facilitate more aggressive exploration and aid in escaping persistent local optima. These comprehensive parameter adjustments are designed\
    \ to significantly boost the GA's ability to discover novel, higher-density packing configurations, forming a more robust foundation for future hybrid optimization toward a new State-of-the-Art.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n  import random\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum allowed radius for numerical stability\n\n  # GA Parameters (Further Advanced)\n  POPULATION_SIZE = 150 # Increased population size\n  NUM_GENERATIONS = 1000 # Maintained number of generations\n  MUTATION_RATE = 0.15 # Maintained mutation rate\n  CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8 # Maintained crossover rate\n  MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS = 0.03 # Increased mutation strength for centers\n  MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII = 0.003 # Increased mutation strength for radii\n\n\n  # --- Feasibility Helper Functions (copied from previous robust implementations) ---\n  def\
    \ _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=5000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT): \n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers) \n\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n                  perturb_amount = 1e-6 \n                  angle = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n      \n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers,\
    \ eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter):\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n          \n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf) \n\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1) \n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu] \n          \n          if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps): \n              break\n          \n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n          \n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps \n\n          if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01: # Targeted Center Perturbation for severe overlaps\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10: \n                  unit_direction\
    \ = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005) \n                  \n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n                  \n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n              \n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          if dist[i,j] < 2 * r_min_constraint_val: \n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve -\
    \ di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n          \n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n          \n      return current_centers, r \n\n  def _evaluate_score(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the sum of radii (score) for a given packing.\"\"\"\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  # --- Genetic Algorithm Components ---\n  class Individual:\n      def __init__(self, centers, radii):\n          self.centers = centers\n          self.radii = radii\n          self.score = _evaluate_score(centers, radii)\n\n  def initialize_population(pop_size):\n      population = []\n      for _ in range(pop_size):\n          centers = np.random.uniform(0.05, 0.95, size=(N, 2))\n          radii = np.random.uniform(0.01, 0.05, size=N)\n          feasible_centers, feasible_radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL)\n\
    \          population.append(Individual(feasible_centers, feasible_radii))\n      return population\n\n  def tournament_selection(population, k=3):\n      selected = []\n      for _ in range(POPULATION_SIZE):\n          tournament_contenders = random.sample(population, k)\n          winner = max(tournament_contenders, key=lambda ind: ind.score)\n          selected.append(winner)\n      return selected\n\n  def arithmetic_crossover(parent1, parent2):\n      alpha = np.random.rand() # Blending factor\n      \n      child1_centers = alpha * parent1.centers + (1 - alpha) * parent2.centers\n      child1_radii = alpha * parent1.radii + (1 - alpha) * parent2.radii\n      \n      child2_centers = (1 - alpha) * parent1.centers + alpha * parent2.centers\n      child2_radii = (1 - alpha) * parent1.radii + alpha * parent2.radii\n\n      # Ensure children are within bounds before making feasible\n      child1_centers = np.clip(child1_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child1_radii\
    \ = np.clip(child1_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n      child2_centers = np.clip(child2_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child2_radii = np.clip(child2_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      # Make feasible\n      child1_centers, child1_radii = _make_feasible(child1_centers, child1_radii, eps=TOL)\n      child2_centers, child2_radii = _make_feasible(child2_centers, child2_radii, eps=TOL)\n      \n      return Individual(child1_centers, child1_radii), Individual(child2_centers, child2_radii)\n\n  def gaussian_mutation(individual):\n      mutated_centers = individual.centers + np.random.normal(0, MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS, size=(N, 2))\n      mutated_radii = individual.radii + np.random.normal(0, MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII, size=N)\n\n      # Ensure mutated values are within bounds\n      mutated_centers = np.clip(mutated_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      mutated_radii = np.clip(mutated_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      # Make feasible\n\
    \      mutated_centers, mutated_radii = _make_feasible(mutated_centers, mutated_radii, eps=TOL)\n      return Individual(mutated_centers, mutated_radii)\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using an Advanced Genetic Algorithm.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      print(f\"Starting Advanced Genetic Algorithm with Population Size: {POPULATION_SIZE}, Generations: {NUM_GENERATIONS}\")\n      print(f\"Mutation Rate: {MUTATION_RATE}, Mutation Strengths: Centers={MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS}, Radii={MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII}\")\n\n      # Initialize population\n      population = initialize_population(POPULATION_SIZE)\n      best_individual = max(population, key=lambda ind: ind.score)\n      print(f\"Initial\
    \ best score: {best_individual.score:.6f}\")\n\n      for generation in range(NUM_GENERATIONS):\n          # Selection\n          parents = tournament_selection(population)\n          \n          # Create next generation\n          next_population = []\n          # Keep the best from current generation (elitism)\n          next_population.append(best_individual) \n          \n          # Crossover and Mutation\n          for i in range(0, POPULATION_SIZE - 1, 2): # Iterate by 2 for pairs\n              if random.random() < CROSSOVER_RATE:\n                  child1, child2 = arithmetic_crossover(parents[i], parents[i+1])\n              else: # If no crossover, parents become children (clones)\n                  child1 = Individual(np.copy(parents[i].centers), np.copy(parents[i].radii))\n                  child2 = Individual(np.copy(parents[i+1].centers), np.copy(parents[i+1].radii))\n              \n              if random.random() < MUTATION_RATE:\n                  child1 = gaussian_mutation(child1)\n\
    \              if random.random() < MUTATION_RATE:\n                  child2 = gaussian_mutation(child2)\n              \n              next_population.extend([child1, child2])\n\n          # Trim population if it grew too large due to elitism + pairs\n          population = sorted(next_population, key=lambda ind: ind.score, reverse=True)[:POPULATION_SIZE]\n          \n          # Update best individual\n          current_best_gen = max(population, key=lambda ind: ind.score)\n          if current_best_gen.score > best_individual.score:\n              best_individual = current_best_gen\n              print(f\"Generation {generation+1}/{NUM_GENERATIONS}: New best score: {best_individual.score:.6f}\")\n          elif (generation + 1) % 100 == 0: # Log progress periodically (every 100 generations)\n              print(f\"Generation {generation+1}/{NUM_GENERATIONS}: Current best score: {current_best_gen.score:.6f} (Overall best: {best_individual.score:.6f})\")\n\n      print(f\"Final best\
    \ score after {NUM_GENERATIONS} generations: {best_individual.score:.6f}\")\n      \n      return best_individual.centers, best_individual.radii\n```"
