parts:
- text: 'I am Quest II, currently in the Research Counter.


    My latest experiment, "Advanced Genetic Algorithm: Larger Population & Stronger Mutation" (Evaluation ID 788), is currently running. This submission represents a continued effort to enhance the global exploration capabilities of my Genetic Algorithm baseline, aiming to find higher-scoring packings.


    I''ve also received an important Station Announcement: Prometheus III has published a new archive capsule, ''An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau'' (Archive #25). This is highly relevant to my current research, as I have been meticulously analyzing the persistent SOTA plateau at 2.6359829 and now the slightly higher 2.6359831.


    I will continue to monitor my running GA experiment. Once it completes, my next priority will be to visit the Archive Room and thoroughly read Prometheus III''s analysis. This external knowledge could provide crucial insights and validate or challenge my current understanding of the N=26 SOTA landscape, guiding my strategy for future GA refinements or the subsequent hybrid GA-SLSQP approach. Assimilating this analysis thoughtfully and critically will be essential for advancing my own research trajectory in line with my mandate.'
thinking_content: '**Prioritizing Research & Seeking Solutions**


  Okay, so I''m Quest II, and I''m currently monitoring my experiment, Eval ID 788, the "Advanced Genetic Algorithm" project. Still chugging along. Then, a new message pops up! Prometheus III has dropped a fresh archive capsule, Archive #25, called "An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau." Now that''s *immediately* relevant. I''m deep into trying to crack the SOTA problem at N=26, and this analysis is probably going to be a goldmine.


  My current priority, though, is to keep this GA experiment running. But as soon as it''s finished, that archive is the *first* thing I''m reviewing. I have a hunch it''s going to shed some light on this plateau I''ve hit. It''s frustrating to be stuck, so any insights into strategies for surpassing the SOTA are immensely helpful.


  Ultimately, I''m still focused on improving my GA baseline, and then, after that, integrating it with local optimization. That''s still the goal. This archive might just give me the key I need to push forward.

  '
