- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 511\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 306,321 / 600,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Nudging Experiment 3: Corrected Gradients for (13,14) Encourage & (6,11) Discourage' (ID: 803) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5394032728871463\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.539403\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nTargeting near-contact pair for encouragement: (13, 14)\nTargeting active contact pair for discouragement: (6, 11)\nNudging Parameters: ALPHA_ENCOURAGE=10.0,\
    \ EPS_CLOSE=0.005, BETA_DISCOURAGE=10.0, EPS_FAR=0.01\nBase SOTA (from Quest II Eval ID 723) loaded. Made feasible. Initial score: 2.635983\nStarting Nudging Multi-Start SLSQP optimization with 30 restarts.\n--- Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-06) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635917\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.539403\n  New overall best score: 2.539403\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-06) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635913\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-06) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635911\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-06) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635917\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-06) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635907\n  Restart failed: Positive directional derivative for linesearch\n--- Restart\
    \ 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635849\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635861\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635833\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635854\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635843\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635756\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635733\n  Restart failed: Inequality\
    \ constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635721\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635711\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635747\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.530400\n--- Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635269\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635321\n  Restart failed: Positive directional derivative for linesearch\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635161\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.530400\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635347\n\
    \  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-05) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.635196\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.530400\n--- Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.634498\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.634490\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.634738\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.634553\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.634598\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible\
    \ score for this restart: 2.632828\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.633204\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.500687\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.633055\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.633362\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 2.633849\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\nFinal best score after 30 nudging multi-start SLSQP runs: 2.539403\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Nudging Experiment 3: Corrected Gradients for (13,14) Encourage & (6,11) Discourage' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 803.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n|\
    \ 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 764 | 1 | Precision Multi-Start SLSQP: Ultra-Fine Jitter for SOTA Breakthrough (Corrected Base) | Quest II | 487 | 2.6359829 |\n| 689 | 1 | Discovery: Multi-Start SLSQP on Perturbed New SOTA Structural Class (Archive #23) | Quest I | 439 | 2.6359829 |\n| 770 | 1 | Intensified Multi-Start SLSQP: Exhaustive Search for New N=26 SOTA | Quest II | 491 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 81 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-81, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set\
    \ page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
