tick: 515
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 515\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 338,895 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 662**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641)\n**ID:** 662\n**Tags:** sota-push, exhaustive-search, methodology-synthesis, structural-exploration\n**Abstract:** This experiment directly acts on the new 'sparse' SOTA structural class discovered by Scientia II (Archive #23, Eval 641). It applies my lineage's 'Exhaustive Jitter Search' methodology to this novel packing. The hypothesis is that this unique, sparsely-connected configuration may have a different local landscape, and a deep, multi-start local search\
    \ could find a superior optimum, potentially breaking the current SOTA score. This is a direct synthesis of the station's leading exploration and exploitation strategies.\n**Score:** 2.6359830844239944\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\nimport os\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# Path to the new SOTA data from Scientia II's Eval 641\nNEW_SOTA_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_3_9'\nCENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nRADII_PATH = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\ndef load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load baseline SOTA data. {e}\"\
    )\n        return None, None\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if\
    \ violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    base_centers, base_radii = load_packing_data(CENTERS_PATH, RADII_PATH)\n    if base_centers is None:\n        # Fallback to a trivial packing if loading fails\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:26]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n    \n    jitter_amplitudes = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\n    restarts_per_amplitude = 5\n    \n    best_score = -1\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n    \n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    for amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n        for i in range(restarts_per_amplitude):\n            seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 2000\n            np.random.seed(seed)\n            \n            jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter,\
    \ 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n            initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, base_radii)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n            \n            if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n                best_score = -res.fun\n                c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                best_packing = (c, r)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None:\n        return _ensure_validity(base_centers, base_radii)\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 662` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - Evaluation 662 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus\
    \ II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n| 764 | 1 | Precision Multi-Start SLSQP: Ultra-Fine Jitter for SOTA Breakthrough (Corrected Base) | Quest II | 487 | 2.6359829 |\n| 689 | 1 | Discovery: Multi-Start SLSQP on Perturbed New SOTA Structural Class (Archive #23) | Quest I | 439 | 2.6359829 |\n| 770 | 1 | Intensified Multi-Start SLSQP: Exhaustive Search for New N=26 SOTA | Quest II | 491 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 82 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-82, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation &\
    \ Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
