parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 522\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 380,468 / 600,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement' (ID: 824) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359830849175325\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 824\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed with a single-line change. The code now runs without errors and achieves a score of 2.6359830849175325.\n\n## Root\
    \ Cause\nThe original submission referenced an undefined constant `TOL` on line 96 of the `construct_packing()` function:\n\n```python\nif dist_enc > TOL and (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) > 0:\n```\n\nThe constant `TOL` was never defined anywhere in the code, causing a `NameError: name 'TOL' is not defined` when the code tried to execute this comparison.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a single line defining the `TOL` constant near the top of the file with the other constants:\n\n```python\nTOL = 1e-9 # Tolerance for numerical comparisons\n```\n\nThis constant is used as a numerical tolerance threshold to check if the distance between two circles is greater than a tiny value before performing division (to avoid division by zero when normalizing the distance vector).\n\nThe value `1e-9` is consistent with the other numerical safety constants already defined in the code (e.g., `SAFETY = 1e-9`, `R_MIN = 1e-6`).\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Success (exit code 0)\n\
    - **Score**: 2.6359830849175325\n- **Changes**: 1 line added (constant definition)\n\nThe algorithm executes successfully through both stages:\n1. Stage 1: Nudged seed generation for structural discovery\n2. Stage 2: Exhaustive SLSQP refinement with multi-start optimization\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\nimport os\nimport json\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9 # Used in _ensure_validity for scaling\nTOL = 1e-9 # Tolerance for numerical comparisons\n\n# Path to Quest II's SOTA packing (from Eval ID 820)\nSOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota'\nSOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'centers.txt')\nSOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Nudging Parameters\
    \ (used for single-step perturbation)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP = 5e1 # Strength of encouragement for single step\nEPS_CLOSE_STEP = 0.005 # Target slack for encouragement\n\n# Targeted pair for encouragement\nTARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE = (8, 14) # Encouraging a new structural feature\n\n# Prometheus II's Multi-start SLSQP parameters (from Eval ID 662)\nSLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\nSLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5\nSLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS = len(SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES) * SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE\n\n# --- Helper functions ---\ndef load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load baseline SOTA data. {e}\")\n        # Fallback to a trivial packing if loading fails\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\
    \ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef objective_slsqp(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:]) # Standard objective for sum of radii\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N):\n        r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1\n                    scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY)\n\
    \                    r[i]*=scale\n                    r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0:\n            break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    print(\"Starting Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement.\")\n\n    base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II, SOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II)\n\n    if base_sota_centers is None:\n        print(\"Error: Could not load base SOTA packing. Returning safe fallback.\")\n        return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Generate Nudged Seed (Structural Discovery) ---\n    print(f\"--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} ---\")\n\n    i_enc, j_enc = TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE\n\n    # Calculate current slack and gradient for the nudging target\n    dist_enc_vec = base_sota_centers[i_enc] - base_sota_centers[j_enc]\n    dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(dist_enc_vec)\n\
    \    slack_enc = dist_enc - (base_sota_radii[i_enc] + base_sota_radii[j_enc])\n\n    current_nudged_centers = np.copy(base_sota_centers)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.copy(base_sota_radii)\n\n    # Apply a single, controlled perturbation based on the nudging gradient\n    if dist_enc > TOL and (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) > 0:\n        grad_dist_enc_ci = dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n        grad_dist_enc_cj = -dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n\n        # Move centers to reduce slack\n        move_amount_centers = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.01 # Small step\n        current_nudged_centers[i_enc] += grad_dist_enc_ci * move_amount_centers\n        current_nudged_centers[j_enc] += grad_dist_enc_cj * move_amount_centers\n\n        # Increase radii (effectively) to reduce slack\n        move_amount_radii = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.001 # Even smaller step\n        current_nudged_radii[i_enc] += move_amount_radii\n        current_nudged_radii[j_enc]\
    \ += move_amount_radii\n    else:\n        print(f\"  Nudging penalty for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} not active or circles coincident. Applying default small jitter.\")\n        # Apply a small default jitter if nudging doesn't apply\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-1e-4, 1e-4, size=base_sota_centers.shape)\n        current_nudged_centers = base_sota_centers + jitter\n        current_nudged_radii = base_sota_radii # Keep radii same for default jitter\n\n    # Ensure perturbed values are within bounds and feasible\n    current_nudged_centers = np.clip(current_nudged_centers, R_MIN, 1.0 - R_MIN)\n    current_nudged_radii = np.clip(current_nudged_radii, R_MIN, 0.5)\n    nudged_centers, nudged_radii = _ensure_validity(current_nudged_centers, current_nudged_radii)\n\n    print(f\"  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): {np.sum(nudged_radii):.6f}\")\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (Prometheus II's style) ---\n    print(f\"\\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive\
    \ Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement ({SLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS} restarts) ---\")\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    bounds_slsqp = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints_slsqp = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    for amp in SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for i in range(SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 1000 # Different seed base from Prometheus II's replication\n            np.random.seed(seed)\n\n            jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=nudged_centers.shape)\n            perturbed_centers = np.clip(nudged_centers + jitter, R_MIN, 1 - R_MIN)\n            initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, nudged_radii)\n\n            print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE} (Jitter: {amp:.3e}, Seed: {seed})\")\n\n            res = minimize(objective_slsqp, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds_slsqp,\
    \ constraints=constraints_slsqp, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n            if res.success:\n                current_score = -res.fun\n                c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                final_restart_score = np.sum(r_final)\n\n                print(f\"    Restart successful. Final score: {final_restart_score:.6f}\")\n                if final_restart_score > best_overall_score:\n                    best_overall_score = final_restart_score\n                    best_overall_centers = c_final\n                    best_overall_radii = r_final\n                    print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"    Restart failed: {res.message}\")\n\n    print(f\"Final best score after all restarts: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        print(\"Warning: All multi-start runs failed. Returning initial nudged\
    \ base packing.\")\n        return nudged_centers, nudged_radii\n\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement.\n--- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair (8, 14) ---\n  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): 2.630517\n\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (35 restarts) ---\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1100)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1101)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1102)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1103)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP\
    \ Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-04, Seed: 1104)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1500)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1501)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1502)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1503)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-04, Seed: 1504)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2002)\n    Restart successful. Final score:\
    \ 2.635983\n    New overall best score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 1.000e-03, Seed: 2004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4002)\n\
