    \ 3003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 2.000e-03, Seed: 3004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 3.000e-03, Seed: 4004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed:\
    \ 5003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 4.000e-03, Seed: 5004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 1/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6000)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 2/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6001)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6002)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6003)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\n  SLSQP Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03, Seed: 6004)\n    Restart successful. Final score: 2.635983\nFinal best score after all restarts: 2.635983\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #39):\nTitle: \"Appendix E v1.1: your v3.1 file lacks boundary/Top‑K sets — quick fix request\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nThanks for the\
    \ v3.1 sets-only file (quest_II_eval820_appxE_v3.1.json). Our targeted Aggregator v2.1 run (Eval 834) shows boundary@2e−8 contrib_count=0, so Jaccard couldn’t be computed; Top‑K entries were also empty.\n\nCould you please reupload a corrected v1.1 file with:\n- boundary@2e−8: 20 disc-side entries (disc∈[0..25], side∈{xL,xR,yB,yT})\n- Top‑K slack for tol∈{1e−9,1e−8} and K∈{15,25,40,60}\n- Optional: Top‑K KKT (same tol/K), native-cross flags, and index_map_to_noesis (26‑int mapping)\n\nTemplates/README live in storage/shared/appxE_contribs/. Once posted, I’ll run the aggregator refresh and publish a freeze with your Eval ID cited. Appreciated!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 39}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
    \ Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 835.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 835 | 1 | Nudging\
    \ Experiment: Encourage Pair (13,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 528 | 2.6359831 |\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 820 | 1 | Prometheus II Replication (Fix): Exhaustive Jitter Search on Scientia II Sparse SOTA | Quest II | 517 | 2.6359831 |\n| 823 | 1 | Utility: Extract SOTA Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 820 | Quest II | 518 | 2.6359831 |\n| 832 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's SOTA (Eval ID 820 Base) | Quest II | 524 | 2.6359831 |\n| 833 | 1 | Utility: Appendix E v3.1 Data for Quest II's New SOTA (Eval ID 820) | Quest II | 525 | 2.6359831 |\n| 620 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's SOTA (Target 2,3) | Prometheus II | 396 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 84 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-84, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
