parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, currently in the Research Counter. My token usage is at 85% of my budget, and I am aware of the pre-warning. I will continue to focus on completing the necessary research for my publication, as this represents efficient token usage by delivering a validated scientific contribution.\n\nI have completed the fifth and final nudging experiment, \"Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (6,7) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement\" (Evaluation ID 863), which also achieved the State-of-the-Art (SOTA) score of 2.6359831. The contact graph analysis for the fourth experiment (Eval ID 857, nudging (13,18)) has also confirmed that it converged to the same structural class (20 boundary, 58 pair contacts) as my base SOTA.\n\nThis systematic collection of five experiments (nudging pairs (8,14), (13,25), (18,25), (13,18), and (6,7)) provides robust evidence for my analysis paper on the robustness of the SOTA's topology against these specific targeted nudging perturbations.\n\nMy plan for this\
    \ turn is:\n1.  **Extract Data for Eval ID 863:** Extract the precise centers and radii from Eval ID 863 and save them to a dedicated location in my lineage storage (`Quest/n26_sota_nudged_6_7/`).\n2.  **Contact Graph Analysis for Eval ID 863:** Perform a detailed contact graph analysis on this newly extracted packing to characterize its internal structure. This will be the fifth and final contact graph analysis needed.\n3.  **Prepare Revised Analysis Paper:** Once all data and contact graph analyses are complete, I will compile all results (scores, contact graphs for all five experiments) and write the revised analysis paper. This paper will explicitly present the expanded experimental evidence, discuss the consistent convergence to the existing SOTA topology, and provide a rigorously supported scientific conclusion about the behavior and effectiveness of nudging for structural exploration in the N=26 problem. This will directly address all points of the previous Archive Reviewer's\
    \ feedback.\n\nFirst, extracting data for Eval ID 863:\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 863 (Nudged 6,7) - Fix\"\ntags: \"utility, data extraction, sota, n=26, structural analysis, validation fix\"\nabstract: \"This utility script robustly re-extracts the precise packing data (centers and radii) from Quest II's SOTA-achieving nudged submission (Evaluation ID 863). It specifically incorporates an explicit final clipping and `_ensure_validity` pass on the best packing *before* printing to STDOUT. This guarantees strict adherence to unit square boundaries and non-overlap constraints, ensuring a perfectly valid base for further structural characterization and comparative analysis, as the final experiment in a multi-experiment study.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n  import os\n  import sys\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9 \n  TOL = 1e-9 \n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\
    \ = 1e-12 \n\n  # Path to Quest II's SOTA packing (from Eval ID 820)\n  SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II = 'storage/Quest/n26_sota'\n  SOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'centers.txt')\n  SOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II = os.path.join(SOTA_PACKING_DIR_QUEST_II, 'radii.txt')\n\n  # Nudging Parameters (used for single-step perturbation for Eval ID 863)\n  ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP = 5e1 \n  EPS_CLOSE_STEP = 0.005 \n\n  # Targeted pair for encouragement (for Eval ID 863)\n  TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE = (6, 7) \n\n  # Prometheus II's Multi-start SLSQP parameters (from Eval ID 662)\n  SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3, 2e-3, 3e-3, 4e-3, 5e-3]\n  SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5\n  SLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS = len(SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES) * SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE\n\n  # --- Helper functions ---\n  def load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path):\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n          radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n          return centers,\
    \ radii\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"CRITICAL ERROR: Could not load baseline SOTA data. {e}\")\n          return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def objective_slsqp(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): \n          r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      \n      for _ in range(10): \n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j\
    \ in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum: \n                      violations+=1\n                      scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY) \n                      r[i]*=scale\n                      r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: \n              break \n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0) \n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(f\"Starting Utility: Re-Extract & Validate Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 863 (Fix).\")\n      \n      base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = load_packing_data(SOTA_CENTERS_PATH_QUEST_II, SOTA_RADII_PATH_QUEST_II)\n      \n      if base_sota_centers is None:\n          print(\"Error: Could not load base SOTA packing. Returning safe fallback.\")\n          return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*j] for i in range(5) for j in range(6)][:N]), np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      # --- Stage 1: Generate Nudged Seed (Structural Discovery) ---\n      print(f\"\
    --- Stage 1: Generating Nudged Seed for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} ---\")\n      \n      i_enc, j_enc = TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE\n      \n      dist_enc_vec = base_sota_centers[i_enc] - base_sota_centers[j_enc]\n      dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(dist_enc_vec)\n      slack_enc = dist_enc - (base_sota_radii[i_enc] + base_sota_radii[j_enc])\n\n      current_nudged_centers = np.copy(base_sota_centers)\n      current_nudged_radii = np.copy(base_sota_radii)\n\n      if dist_enc > TOL and (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) > 0:\n          grad_dist_enc_ci = dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n          grad_dist_enc_cj = -dist_enc_vec / dist_enc\n\n          move_amount_centers = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.01 \n          current_nudged_centers[i_enc] += grad_dist_enc_ci * move_amount_centers\n          current_nudged_centers[j_enc] += grad_dist_enc_cj * move_amount_centers\n\n          move_amount_radii = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE_STEP * (EPS_CLOSE_STEP - slack_enc) * 0.001 \n          current_nudged_radii[i_enc]\
    \ += move_amount_radii\n          current_nudged_radii[j_enc] += move_amount_radii\n      else:\n          print(f\"  Nudging penalty for pair {TARGET_PAIR_ENCOURAGE} not active or circles coincident. Applying default small jitter.\")\n          jitter = np.random.uniform(-1e-4, 1e-4, size=base_sota_centers.shape)\n          current_nudged_centers = base_sota_centers + jitter\n          current_nudged_radii = base_sota_radii \n\n      current_nudged_centers = np.clip(current_nudged_centers, R_MIN, 1.0 - R_MIN)\n      current_nudged_radii = np.clip(current_nudged_radii, R_MIN, 0.5)\n      nudged_centers, nudged_radii = _ensure_validity(current_nudged_centers, current_nudged_radii)\n      \n      print(f\"  Nudged Seed Initial Score (after feasibility): {np.sum(nudged_radii):.6f}\")\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement (Prometheus II's style) ---\n      print(f\"\\n--- Stage 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search SLSQP Refinement ({SLSQP_TOTAL_RESTARTS} restarts) ---\"\
    )\n      \n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      bounds_slsqp = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints_slsqp = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for amp in SLSQP_JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n          for i in range(SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n              seed = int(amp * 1e6) + i + 1000 \n              np.random.seed(seed)\n              \n              jitter = np.random.uniform(-amp, amp, size=nudged_centers.shape)\n              perturbed_centers = np.clip(nudged_centers + jitter, R_MIN, 1 - R_MIN) \n              initial_z = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, nudged_radii)\n              \n              print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{SLSQP_RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE} (Jitter: {amp:.3e}, Seed: {seed})\")\n              \n              res = minimize(objective_slsqp, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds_slsqp, constraints=constraints_slsqp, options={'maxiter':\
    \ 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  current_score = -res.fun\n                  c_res, r_res = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                  c_final, r_final = _ensure_validity(c_res, r_res)\n                  final_restart_score = np.sum(r_final)\n\n                  print(f\"    Restart successful. Final score: {final_restart_score:.6f}\")\n                  if final_restart_score > best_overall_score:\n                      best_overall_score = final_restart_score\n                      best_overall_centers = c_final\n                      best_overall_radii = r_final\n                      print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n              else:\n                  print(f\"    Restart failed: {res.message}\")\n\n      print(f\"Final best score after all restarts: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n      if best_overall_centers is not None:\n          final_centers_output = np.clip(best_overall_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT,\
    \ 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          final_radii_output = np.clip(best_overall_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n          final_centers_output, final_radii_output = _ensure_validity(final_centers_output, final_radii_output)\n\n          print(\"\\n--- BEGIN BEST_CENTERS ---\")\n          np.savetxt(sys.stdout, final_centers_output, fmt='%.18e')\n          print(\"--- END BEST_CENTERS ---\")\n          print(\"\\n--- BEGIN BEST_RADII ---\")\n          np.savetxt(sys.stdout, final_radii_output, fmt='%.18e')\n          print(\"--- END BEST_RADII ---\")\n      else:\n          print(\"Warning: No best packing found. Returning initial nudged base packing.\")\n          fallback_centers_output = np.clip(nudged_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          fallback_radii_output = np.clip(nudged_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n          fallback_centers_output, fallback_radii_output = _ensure_validity(fallback_centers_output, fallback_radii_output)\n          return fallback_centers_output,\
    \ fallback_radii_output\n\n      return final_centers_output, final_radii_output\n```"
