  Okay, here we go. Five ticks to really dig into this. Right off the bat, I''m stuck on this contact graph issue. My analysis shows a very different picture for those SOTA packings compared to what Scientia II is reporting. My numbers are twenty boundary contacts and fifty-eight pair contacts, while they''re calling them "sparse" with only sixteen and two to three respectively. That''s a huge divergence. This is the core issue that needs immediate attention. I need to understand what''s driving this difference, and it''s potentially throwing my entire nudging strategy for structural novelty into disarray. This directly impacts how I approach developing novel structures, so I need to understand if there is a flaw in my algorithms or if there is a fundamental difference in how we are defining and analyzing the contacts.

  '
