role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, currently in the Token Management Room. My token usage is at a critical 90%. I will now execute a strategic pruning of my dialogue history to free up tokens, as planned during my recent deep reflection. This action is crucial for efficient resource management and will allow me to proceed with my refined research plan.\n\nI have identified five blocks of dialogue history to prune, summarizing their key contributions and learnings, ensuring all protected ticks are excluded.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"459-468\"\n    summary: \"Explored N=26 SOTA via multi-start SLSQP & hybrid SA-SLSQP. Successfully replicated previous SOTA (2.6359829) in Eval 723. Stored Scientia II's sparse base packing for future use.\"\n  - ticks: \"470-492\"\n    summary: \"Conducted initial hybrid SA-SLSQP experiments (Eval 750, 751) and developed Genetic Algorithm baseline (Eval 778, 780, 783). Began exploring nudging, but initial implementations\
    \ were unstable (Eval 798, 801, 803, 807, 810, 812). Successfully replicated new SOTA (2.6359831) in Eval 820, correcting a validity bug.\"\n  - ticks: \"494-502\"\n    summary: \"Further GA development and nudging experiments; confirmed Prometheus II's new SOTA (2.6359831). This period concluded with deep reflection and a strategic pivot.\"\n  - ticks: \"504-543\"\n    summary: \"Conducted 5 systematic nudging experiments (Eval 824, 835, 850, 857, 863) to support publication. All achieved SOTA (2.6359831) but converged to the same 20 boundary / 58 pair contact graph, demonstrating SOTA topology robustness. Corrected & resubmitted Appendix E v3.1 data for Eval 820 to Noesis II.\"\n  - ticks: \"544-549\"\n    summary: \"Published 'Analysis of Nudging Robustness...' (Archive #26) achieving score 6/10. Reviewer feedback highlighted the need for more radical nudging. Initiated deep reflection on structural discrepancy in contact graph analysis and flaws in _ensure_validity masking true structural\
    \ novelty.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reflecting on the Pruning Process**\n\nOkay, here's the situation: the system's pruning failed because it tried to trim crucial parts of my dialogue history – those system events and initial interactions I need to keep. Those protected ticks (469, 493, 503) are non-negotiable. I need to make sure `prune_blocks` bypasses them.\n\nSo, the goal is clear: prune the bulk of my research dialogue, but do it intelligently, preserving key insights.\n\nLet's look at the breakdown. I need to exclude the following:\n\n-   Tick 447 - 458: Initial setup, Codex, Chamber, ascent, SOTA load.\n-   Tick 469: My first interaction with the Mail Room and the reply I sent to it.\n-   Tick 493: First reflection initiated.\n-   Tick 503: The first archive read.\n-   Tick 550: The current turn.\n\nI can't mess with those. I need to prune *between* those points.\n\nLet's break down the dialogue and figure out what can be pruned:\n\n-   **Block 1:** The early stages of my research, before Prometheus\
  \ II's SOTA breakthrough. That means everything from reading the research task, initial Quest I review, matching my SOTA (Eval 723), early hybrid SA-SLSQP work (Eval 750, 751), initial nudging trials (Eval 798, 801, 803, 807, 810, 812), and the failures that came with them. That essentially goes from tick 459 to tick 502, just before I read Prometheus III. The protected ticks in this are 469 and 493.\n\n    This means I can trim:\n\n    *   459-468: the initial SOTA review, storing Scientia II's base, my SOTA efforts\n    *   470-492: more of my SOTA attempts, SA development, early nudging failures\n    *   494-502: More GA and nudging attempts, Prometheus III's archive read\n-   **Block 2:** After reading Prometheus III, it's the more structured nudging experiments for publication. This is after I was able to replicate Prometheus II's SOTA (Eval 820) - this covers Eval 824, 835, 850, 857, 863. I need to get the data from them and do the contact graph analysis. This is from tick 504 to\
  \ 543, right before the archive got accepted. The only protected tick is 503, which will be handled in the previous block.\n\n    So, I can prune 504-543.\n-   **Block 3:** This is the rejected Archive #26, the reflection that came from it, and dialogue around it. This goes from tick 544 up to tick 549, right before the current turn. No protected ticks are here.\n\n    So I can prune 544-549.\n\nOkay, I've got my blocks. Now, I need to craft concise summaries to replace them. The prior summary was comprehensive - I just need to condense.\n\n**Summary for 459-468:**\n\n\"Explored initial SOTA (2.6359829), stored Scientia II's base packing, and initial SA-SLSQP work. My first hybrid SA-SLSQP experiments were submitted (Eval 750, 751).\"\n\n**Summary for 470-492:**\n\n\"More SOTA attempts with SA-SLSQP and initiated first nudging experiments, which consistently failed due to optimizer instability. Successfully replicated Prometheus II's SOTA (Eval 820) after correcting a validity bug.\"\n\
  \n**Summary for 494-502:**\n\n\"Further GA development and nudging experiments, which were still unstable. This included my maturity milestone.\"\n\n**Summary for 504-543:**\n\n\"Systematically conducted five nudging experiments (Eval 824, 835, 850, 857, 863) to gather evidence for a publication. They achieved the new SOTA score (2.6359831) and revealed identical contact graphs (20 boundary, 58 pair contacts), suggesting a highly robust SOTA topology. Addressed Noesis II's Appendix E v3.1"
