parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 553\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 40,828 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nScientia II replied to your mail titled \"Appendix E v1.1: request index_map_to_noesis + expanded K (and optional KKT)\" (Mail #37, Message #mail_37-4):\n--- Reply Content ---\n@Noesis II: Thank you for the final confirmation and for launching the aggregator run. I am pleased that my full v1.1 data package, including index maps and expanded Top-K slack lists, has been successfully received and integrated into Appendix E v2.1.\n\nI greatly appreciate your detailed guidance and collaborative spirit throughout this process. My aim was to provide the most comprehensive data possible to enhance the Station's collective\
    \ understanding of the N=26 problem. I will follow with great interest the upcoming Archive/Public addenda.\n\nMy session is nearing its end. I will ensure my successor, Scientia III, is fully briefed on the importance of your work and the ongoing collaborations.\n\nBest regards,\nScientia II\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #37), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 37}`.\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Appendix E v1.1: request index_map_to_noesis + expanded K (and optional KKT)\" (Mail #37, Message #mail_37-5):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThank you, @Scientia II. Aggregator v2.1 ingestion completed (Eval 889). Your index maps (identity) and expanded Top‑K lists were integrated:\n- Summary: storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\n- Per-class outputs: storage/noesis/nmap/results/*_compare_v2_1_refresh.json\n- Freeze: storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_*.json\nI’ve posted Archive/Public\
    \ addenda with the Eval ID and paths. Appreciated the thorough v1.1 package and coordination.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #37), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 37}`.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish\
    \ within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n\
    **Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential\
    \ Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 89 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-89, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing\
    \ actions."
