tick: 557
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, currently in the Research Counter. My previous Genetic Algorithm baseline (Eval ID 891) demonstrated the GA's capability for global search but yielded a score significantly below SOTA.\n\nFollowing my research plan, I will now focus on parameter tuning to improve its performance. I will submit a new experiment with increased population size and number of generations to allow for more extensive exploration and convergence.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GA Parameter Tuning: Increased Population & Generations\"\ntags: \"genetic algorithm, parameter tuning, N=26\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tunes the Genetic Algorithm baseline (Eval ID 891) by increasing the population size to 100 and the number of generations to 200. The objective is to evaluate if expanded search resources can lead to higher scores and better exploration of the N=26 circle packing landscape, while keeping other genetic parameters constant.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\
    \  import random\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum allowed radius for numerical stability\n\n  # Re-incorporate feasibility helpers from previous high-scoring submissions\n  def _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=TOL, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter=5000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers)\n\n      # Initial perturbation for identical centers\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n          \
    \        perturb_amount = 1e-6\n                  angle = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter):\n          # Calculate distances between centers\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf) # Ignore self-distances\n\n          # Find overlaps\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1) # Upper triangle indices, excluding diagonal\n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu]\n\n       \
    \   if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps): # No significant overlaps\n              break\n\n          # Resolve the largest overlap\n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n\n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps # Add a small buffer\n\n          # Perturb centers for severe overlaps to prevent sticking\n          if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01:\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10:\n                  unit_direction = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005) # Small, controlled move\n\n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n\n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\
    \                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          # Shrink radii to resolve overlap\n          if dist[i,j] < 2 * r_min_constraint_val: # If circles are almost at the same point, minimize their radii\n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              # Distribute overlap reduction proportionally to radii\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n\n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r,\
    \ r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      return current_centers, r\n\n  # Individual representation: a tuple of (centers, radii)\n  def create_individual():\n      centers = np.random.uniform(0.1, 0.9, size=(N, 2)) # Initial centers slightly within bounds\n      radii = np.random.uniform(R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.1, size=N) # Small initial radii\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii) # Ensure initial feasibility\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def calculate_fitness(individual):\n      centers, radii = individual\n      # The system's _evaluate function will validate. Here, we maximize sum of radii.\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def select_parents(population, fitnesses, k=2): # Tournament selection\n      selected_parents = []\n      for _ in range(k):\n          tournament_candidates = random.sample(list(zip(population, fitnesses)), min(3, len(population))) # Select min(3, pop_size) random individuals\n          winner = max(tournament_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0] # Choose\
    \ the one with highest fitness\n          selected_parents.append(winner)\n      return selected_parents\n\n  def crossover(parent1, parent2): # Simple arithmetic crossover for centers and radii\n      centers1, radii1 = parent1\n      centers2, radii2 = parent2\n\n      alpha = np.random.uniform(0, 1)\n      child_centers = alpha * centers1 + (1 - alpha) * centers2\n      child_radii = alpha * radii1 + (1 - alpha) * radii2\n\n      # Clamp to valid ranges before making feasible to avoid extreme values\n      child_centers = np.clip(child_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child_radii = np.clip(child_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      child_centers, child_radii = _make_feasible(child_centers, child_radii)\n      return child_centers, child_radii\n\n  def mutate(individual, mutation_rate, mutation_strength=0.01): # Gaussian mutation\n      centers, radii = individual\n      \n      # Mutate centers\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n\
    \              centers[i, 0] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength)\n              centers[i, 1] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength)\n      centers = np.clip(centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n      # Mutate radii\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              radii[i] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength * 0.1) # Smaller mutation for radii\n      radii = np.clip(radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii) # Ensure feasibility after mutation\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # GA Parameters - Tuned for this experiment\n      POP_SIZE = 100 # Increased from 50\n      NUM_GENERATIONS = 200 # Increased from 100\n      MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\n      CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8\n      MUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.01 \n\n      print(f\"Starting Genetic Algorithm with {POP_SIZE} population and {NUM_GENERATIONS} generations.\")\n\n      # Initialization\n\
    \      population = [create_individual() for _ in range(POP_SIZE)]\n      best_overall_packing = None\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n\n      for generation in range(NUM_GENERATIONS):\n          fitnesses = [calculate_fitness(ind) for ind in population]\n\n          # Update best overall\n          current_best_idx = np.argmax(fitnesses)\n          current_best_score = fitnesses[current_best_idx]\n          \n          if current_best_score > best_overall_score:\n              best_overall_score = current_best_score\n              best_overall_packing = population[current_best_idx]\n              print(f\"Gen {generation+1}: New best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n          # else:\n              # print(f\"Gen {generation+1}: Current best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\") # Suppressed for brevity\n\n          new_population = []\n          # Elitism: Keep the best individual\n          if best_overall_packing is not None:\n              new_population.append(best_overall_packing)\n\
    \n          # Generate offspring\n          while len(new_population) < POP_SIZE:\n              parent1, parent2 = select_parents(population, fitnesses)\n              \n              if random.random() < CROSSOVER_RATE:\n                  child_centers, child_radii = crossover(parent1, parent2)\n                  child = (child_centers, child_radii)\n              else:\n                  child = random.choice([parent1, parent2]) # If no crossover, pick one parent\n\n              child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut = mutate(child, MUTATION_RATE, MUTATION_STRENGTH)\n              new_population.append((child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut))\n          \n          population = new_population\n\n      print(f\"Genetic Algorithm finished. Final best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n      \n      if best_overall_packing is None:\n          # Fallback to a trivial packing if somehow no packing was found\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT]\
    \ * N)\n          return centers, radii\n\n      return best_overall_packing\n```"
thinking_content: '**Tuning the Genetic Algorithm for Improved Performance**


  Okay, so I''ve established a good baseline with the initial Genetic Algorithm run, Quest II is my name. Now it''s time to refine this sucker. Memory Capsule #7 is pulling up my "Next Steps" list for the GA, and I''m zeroing in on **Parameter Tuning** as my initial move. The goal is clear: optimize the convergence speed and, more importantly, the final score.


  I need to start experimenting. Right now, I''m thinking of focusing on population size and the number of generations, seeing how a bigger computational budget impacts the results. My initial parameters have a `POP_SIZE` of 50 and `NUM_GENERATIONS` of 100. I''m going to cautiously increase these to `POP_SIZE = 100` and `NUM_GENERATIONS = 200`. It''s a sensible jump, and it should reveal whether the GA can reach better solutions with more time and candidates. To isolate the effects, I''ll keep the other parameters – mutation and crossover rates, mutation strength – constant for this round. Once I''ve got my updated results, I will refine the tags and abstract to reflect this parameter tuning experiment. Time to get to work!

  '
