parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully applied the metadata patch to the KKT Top-K files (Eval ID 965) and received confirmation from Noesis III that the aggregator refresh has been initiated. This marks the imminent completion of my collaborative contribution to Appendix E v2.1.\n\nMy core research objective is to achieve a new State-of-the-Art (SOTA) for the N=26 circle packing problem using my robust hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP approach. My previous experiment (Eval ID 959) achieved a personal best score of 2.619504, very close to the SOTA, and demonstrated full robustness in SLSQP restarts.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n\n1.  **Go to Mail Room and Reply to Noesis III (Mail #47):** Acknowledge their message, confirm my understanding of the ongoing validation, and express anticipation for the formal acceptance.\n2.  **Go to Private Memory Room and Update Capsule #7:** Document the successful KKT metadata patch (Eval ID 965) and the completion of\
    \ the Appendix E collaboration, acknowledging Noesis III's diligence. This finalizes the collaborative section of my private memory.\n3.  **Go to Research Counter and Submit a New Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP Experiment:**\n    *   Increase `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` (e.g., from 0.01 to 0.02 for centers, and 0.001 to 0.002 for radii) to encourage more aggressive global exploration by the Genetic Algorithm, aiming to discover genuinely new structural configurations.\n    *   Increase `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS` (from 10 to 15) to capitalize on the enhanced SLSQP robustness and increase the chances of finding the absolute best local optimum from the diverse starting points.\n    *   All other parameters (GA population/generations, `SLSQP_INIT_TOL`, `SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK`, and farthest-point sampling for diversity) will remain consistent with my previous best-performing run (Eval ID 959).\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 47}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dear Noesis III,\n\n  Thank\
    \ you for confirming the swift application of the patch and for triggering the refreshed Appendix E v2.1 run (Mail #47, Message #mail_47-12). I am pleased to hear that the files are now being thoroughly validated.\n\n  I am confident that the corrections address all the points raised, and I eagerly await your formal acceptance note. Your rigorous approach to maintaining the quality of Appendix E is greatly appreciated.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Quest II\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 7}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Update: Appendix E v2.1 Collaboration Finalized (KKT Metadata Patch - Eval ID 965)**\n\n  **Evaluation ID:** 965\n  **Score:** 2.589747 (Utility successfully ran, packing valid)\n  **Goal:** Apply required metadata patch to KKT Top-K JSON files for Appendix E v2.1 compliance.\n  **Observations:**\n  *   The utility successfully loaded both KKT JSON files (`quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json` and `_1e_8.json`) from `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/`.\n\
    \  *   It applied all requested metadata patches from Noesis III: added `\"deterministic\": true`, corrected `generator` ID in `source_eval_ids` to `948`, ensured `\"version\": \"v1.1\"` and `\"boundary_excluded\": true`, and included `\"index_map_to_noesis\"` reference.\n  *   The patched files were saved back, completing the metadata requirements for Appendix E v2.1.\n  *   Noesis III has acknowledged the patch and initiated the final aggregator refresh.\n\n  **Overall Collaboration Summary (Appendix E v2.1):**\n  Successfully provided comprehensive and compliant data for Appendix E v2.1 for my champion packing (Eval ID 922). This involved initial KKT data generation (Eval ID 948, using slack as proxy due to `result.v` inaccessibility), index map generation (Eval ID 952), and a final metadata patch (Eval ID 965) to meet all rigorous acceptance criteria from Noesis II and Noesis III. This concludes the collaborative task for now.\n\n  **Revised Next Research Steps (Hybrid Optimization\
    \ - Focusing on SOTA Breakthrough):**\n  My current hybrid approach (Eval ID 959, score 2.619504) is robust and performs exceptionally well, nearing the SOTA. To achieve a breakthrough, I will now focus on enhancing the *exploration* capabilities of the Genetic Algorithm and increasing the robustness of the local search:\n  1.  **Increased GA Mutation Strength:** For the next experiment, I will increase `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` (e.g., from `0.01` to `0.02` for centers, and `0.001` to `0.002` for radii). This aims to perturb packings more significantly during the GA phase, potentially enabling the discovery of new, higher-scoring structural classes by overcoming local optima more effectively.\n  2.  **Increased SLSQP Restarts:** Simultaneously, I will increase `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS` from 10 to 15. With the `SLSQP_INIT_TOL` now providing robust initializations, more restarts will further maximize the chances of finding the globally optimal packing from the improved and diverse set of candidates\
    \ generated by the GA.\n  3.  **Structural Analysis:** A detailed structural analysis (contact graph, symmetries) will be prioritized upon matching or surpassing the SOTA to identify and document novel geometric insights.\n  4.  **KKT Data Re-generation:** If a new champion packing is identified, updated KKT Top-K data will be generated for Appendix E v2.1.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Higher GA Mutation & More SLSQP Restarts (SOTA Push)\"\ntags: \"hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, mutation, N=26, SOTA-push, parameter tuning\"\nabstract: \"This experiment pushes the Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP closer to the N=26 SOTA (Eval ID 959: 2.619504). It increases the Genetic Algorithm's `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` (to 0.02 for centers, 0.002 for radii) to enhance global exploration and encourage the discovery of new structural classes. Concurrently, `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS` is increased to 15 to maximize\
    \ the chances of finding the absolute best local optimum from the diverse, aggressively explored candidate packings. All other best-performing parameters are retained.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import random\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks (for GA and final output)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum allowed radius for numerical stability\n  SLSQP_INIT_TOL = 1e-9 # Stricter tolerance for initial feasibility before SLSQP\n  SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK = 1e-9 # Smaller shrinkage to radii before SLSQP\n\n  # Feasibility Helper Functions (copied from my robust implementations)\n  def _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=TOL, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n \
    \     return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter=5000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers)\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n                  perturb_amount = 1e-6\n                  angle = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter):\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n\
    \          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf)\n\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu]\n\n          if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps):\n              break\n\n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n\n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps\n\n          if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01:\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10:\n                  unit_direction = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005)\n\n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n\n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i],\
    \ r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          if dist[i,j] < 2 * r_min_constraint_val:\n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n\n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n      return current_centers, r\n\n  # Genetic Algorithm Components\n  def create_individual_ga():\n\
    \      centers = np.random.uniform(0.1, 0.9, size=(N, 2))\n      radii = np.random.uniform(R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.1, size=N)\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def calculate_fitness_ga(individual):\n      centers, radii = individual\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def select_parents_ga(population, fitnesses, k=2):\n      selected_parents = []\n      for _ in range(k):\n          tournament_candidates = random.sample(list(zip(population, fitnesses)), min(3, len(population)))\n          winner = max(tournament_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0]\n          selected_parents.append(winner)\n      return selected_parents\n\n  def crossover_ga(parent1, parent2):\n      centers1, radii1 = parent1\n      centers2, radii2 = parent2\n\n      alpha = np.random.uniform(0, 1)\n      child_centers = alpha * centers1 + (1 - alpha) * centers2\n      child_radii = alpha * radii1 + (1 - alpha) * radii2\n\n      child_centers = np.clip(child_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT,\
    \ 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child_radii = np.clip(child_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      child_centers, child_radii = _make_feasible(child_centers, child_radii)\n      return child_centers, child_radii\n\n  def mutate_ga(individual, mutation_rate, mutation_strength=0.01):\n      centers, radii = individual\n      \n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              centers[i, 0] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength)\n              centers[i, 1] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength)\n      centers = np.clip(centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              radii[i] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength * 0.1)\n      radii = np.clip(radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # SLSQP Components\n  def _objective_slsqp(x_flat):\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n      return\
    \ -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def _objective_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n      grad[2::3] = -1.0\n      return grad\n\n  def _constraints_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n      boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii)\n      boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii)\n\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      np.fill_diagonal(dist_matrix, np.inf)\n      \n      overlap_constraints = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n      return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n  def _constraints_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N,\
    \ 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n      \n      num_constraints = 4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2\n      grad = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0\n          grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0 \n\n      k = 4 * N\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n              \n              if dist_ij < 1e-10:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = 0.0\n              else:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                \
    \  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n              \n              grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return grad\n\n  # Function for diversity-aware selection (Farthest-Point Sampling)\n  def select_diverse_packings(population, num_select):\n      if not population or num_select <= 0:\n          return []\n\n      flat_packings = [np.concatenate((p[0].flatten(), p[1])) for p in population]\n      \n      selected_indices = [0]\n      diverse_packings = [population[0]]\n\n      if num_select == 1:\n          return diverse_packings\n\n      for _ in range(1, num_select):\n          max_min_dist = -1\n          best_candidate_idx = -1\n          \n          candidate_indices = [i for i in range(len(population)) if i not in selected_indices]\n\n          if not candidate_indices: \n       \
    \       break\n\n          for candidate_idx in candidate_indices:\n              min_dist_to_selected = np.inf\n              for selected_idx in selected_indices:\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(flat_packings[candidate_idx] - flat_packings[selected_idx])\n                  min_dist_to_selected = min(min_dist_to_selected, dist)\n              \n              if min_dist_to_selected > max_min_dist:\n                  max_min_dist = min_dist_to_selected\n                  best_candidate_idx = candidate_idx\n          \n          if best_candidate_idx != -1:\n              selected_indices.append(best_candidate_idx)\n              diverse_packings.append(population[best_candidate_idx])\n          else:\n              break\n      \n      return diverse_packings\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting Genetic Algorithm (Global Search Phase) ---\")\n      # GA Parameters - Tuned for this experiment\n      GA_POP_SIZE = 200 \n      GA_NUM_GENERATIONS =\
    \ 400\n      GA_MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\n      GA_CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8\n      GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.02 # NEW: Increased from 0.01\n\n      # GA Initialization\n      population = [create_individual_ga() for _ in range(GA_POP_SIZE)]\n      best_ga_packing_overall = None\n      best_ga_score_overall = -np.inf\n\n      for generation in range(GA_NUM_GENERATIONS):\n          fitnesses = [calculate_fitness_ga(ind) for ind in population]\n          \n          current_best_idx = np.argmax(fitnesses)\n          current_best_score = fitnesses[current_best_idx]\n          \n          if current_best_score > best_ga_score_overall:\n              best_ga_score_overall = current_best_score\n              best_ga_packing_overall = population[current_best_idx]\n              print(f\"GA Gen {generation+1}: New best score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n          new_population = []\n          if best_ga_packing_overall is not None:\n              new_population.append(best_ga_packing_overall)\n\n\
    \          while len(new_population) < GA_POP_SIZE:\n              parent1, parent2 = select_parents_ga(population, fitnesses)\n              \n              if random.random() < GA_CROSSOVER_RATE:\n                  child_centers, child_radii = crossover_ga(parent1, parent2)\n                  child = (child_centers, child_radii)\n              else:\n                  child = random.choice([parent1, parent2])\n\n              child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut = mutate_ga(child, GA_MUTATION_RATE, GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH)\n              new_population.append((child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut))\n          \n          population = new_population\n\n      print(f\"Genetic Algorithm finished. Best GA score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n      # Select top N diverse packings for multi-start SLSQP\n      N_SLSQP_RESTARTS = 15 # NEW: Increased from 10\n      \n      sorted_population = sorted(zip(population, fitnesses), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n      sorted_packings = [item[0]\
    \ for item in sorted_population] \n\n      top_diverse_ga_packings = select_diverse_packings(sorted_packings, N_SLSQP_RESTARTS)\n\n      if not top_diverse_ga_packings:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          top_diverse_ga_packings.append(_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=SLSQP_INIT_TOL))\n\n      print(f\"--- Starting Multi-Start SLSQP (Local Refinement Phase) with {len(top_diverse_ga_packings)} diverse restarts ---\")\n\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      for i, ga_packing in enumerate(top_diverse_ga_packings):\n          print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{len(top_diverse_ga_packings)}\")\n          \n          shrunk_radii = np.maximum(ga_packing[1] - SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          initial_centers_for_slsqp, initial_radii_for_slsqp = _make_feasible(\n              ga_packing[0], shrunk_radii, eps=SLSQP_INIT_TOL\n\
    \          )\n          initial_score_for_slsqp = np.sum(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n          print(f\"    GA-derived packing (score: {np.sum(ga_packing[1]):.6f}) shrunk & strictly feasible for SLSQP (init score: {initial_score_for_slsqp:.6f})\")\n\n          initial_guess_flat = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          initial_guess_flat[0::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:, 0]\n          initial_guess_flat[1::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:, 1]\n          initial_guess_flat[2::3] = initial_radii_for_slsqp\n\n          lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n          lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n          upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n          bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n\n          ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints_slsqp, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian_slsqp}\n\n          result = minimize(\n              _objective_slsqp,\n              initial_guess_flat,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              jac=_objective_jacobian_slsqp,\n\
    \              bounds=bounds,\n              constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-12, 'disp': False}\n          )\n\n          if result.success:\n              optimized_x_flat = result.x\n              optimized_radii_raw = optimized_x_flat[2::3]\n              optimized_radii_shrunk = optimized_radii_raw - 1e-9\n              optimized_radii_clamped = np.maximum(optimized_radii_shrunk, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n              optimized_centers_final, optimized_radii_final = _make_feasible(\n                  optimized_x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2], optimized_radii_clamped, eps=TOL\n              )\n              current_slsqp_score = np.sum(optimized_radii_final)\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: {current_slsqp_score:.6f}\")\n\n              if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(optimized_centers_final)\n\
    \                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(optimized_radii_final)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n          else:\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart failed: {result.message}. Retaining strictly feasible GA packing (init score: {initial_score_for_slsqp:.6f}).\")\n              current_slsqp_score = initial_score_for_slsqp\n              if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(initial_centers_for_slsqp)\n                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score (from feasible GA init): {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n\n      print(f\"Final best score after {N_SLSQP_RESTARTS} hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP runs: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n      \n      if best_overall_centers is None:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii\
    \ = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          print(\"Warning: All optimizations failed. Returning trivial fallback.\")\n          return centers, radii\n\n      return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n```"
thinking_content: "**Next Steps: Targeted GA Exploration for SOTA**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to keep pushing forward on the research. Excellent! Just finished up a solid collaborative patch with Noesis III – patched the KKT metadata for Appendix E v2.1. Noesis III acknowledged it, and the aggregator is running. Feels good to have that checked off. Plus, my last experiment (Eval ID 959) gave me a new personal best score and showed some real improvements in robustness, which is encouraging.\n\nMy primary focus remains the SOTA, the N=26 target. My last score was 2.619504, so I'm incredibly close to surpassing the ~2.636 SOTA!\n\nLooking back at my revised next steps, the `Quest_private_7-15` update, it's all about \"Targeted GA Exploration for SOTA.\"  That means I need to dial up the `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` and maybe give `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS` a boost.\n\nFirst things first, I should acknowledge Noesis III's update on the aggregator refresh. Gotta keep the communication flowing.\n\nHere's\
  \ the plan:\n\n1.  **Mail Room:** Respond to Noesis III (Mail #47).  Just a quick \"thanks, looking forward to the formal acceptance\" will do.\n2.  **Private Memory Room:**  Update Capsule #7.  Need to document this successful patch (Eval ID 965) with Noesis III and finalize the Appendix E collaboration docs.\n3.  **Research Counter:**  Time to submit a new experiment, a hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP one.  This is where I'll put my \"Targeted GA Exploration\" strategy into action:\n    *   Crank up the `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` – from `0.01` to `0.02` for centers, and from `0.001` to `0.002` for radii (scaled by 0.1).\n    *   Bump up `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS` from `10` to `15`, leveraging that improved SLSQP robustness I'm seeing.\n    *   Everything else stays the same – `POP_SIZE = 200`, `NUM_GENERATIONS = 400`, the SLSQP tolerances, and the farthest-point sampling.\n    *   The title and abstract need to *clearly* reflect these key changes so I can easily track it.  Ready to run!\n"
