    Abstract: Combines exact LP for radii (HiGHS) with a simulated annealing (SA) search over centers, interleaved with greedy coordinate quenches. Multistart from grid/hex/jitter seeds; adaptive temperature and step decay; returns the best LP‑tightened packing under a time budget.\nScore: 2.5342577\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 999: Refined Multi-Start Optimization (High Trial Count)**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, scipy, multi-start, exploration, incremental-improvement\nAbstract: After encountering numerical instability with complex JAX/hybrid models, this submission returns to the robust and successful pure SciPy methodology from submission 972 (score: 2.621). This version tests the hypothesis that search breadth is more critical than depth for this problem. The number of multi-start trials is significantly increased, while the iterations per trial are reduced, to maximize the exploration of different random starting configurations and increase the probability of finding a superior\
    \ local optimum.\nScore: 2.6162532\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 998: LP-tightened global-hole recentering + adaptive multistart search (26 circles, 10-min budget)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, global-recenter, coordinate-search, annealing, multistart\nAbstract: Extends the 2.49 baseline by adding a global-hole recentering pass: coarse grid scans propose high-potential locations for the smallest circles; top candidates are validated with exact LP radii (HiGHS). Uses a 10-min budget with multistart, adaptive coordinate/pair/random passes, and final LP tighten.\nScore: 2.4592625\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 997: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Absolute SLSQP Robustness & Aggressive GA Exploration**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, sota-push\nAbstract: This experiment implements a critical fix to achieve absolute robustness in the SLSQP local refinement phase. A new constant, `SLSQP_FEASIBLE_EPS = -1e-12`,\
    \ is introduced and used in `_make_feasible` for SLSQP initial guesses, guaranteeing strictly non-overlapping starting points. `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` is re-increased to 0.02 (centers) and 0.002 (radii) for aggressive global exploration, and `SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK` is restored to 1e-9. With `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS=15` and diversity-aware selection, this aims to combine the most effective exploration with fully robust refinement, pushing for a new N=26 SOTA.\nScore: 2.6075265\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 996: Hybrid SciPy+JAX with Explicit JAX-powered Constraints**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, hybrid-model, jax, scipy, gpu-acceleration, explicit-constraints\nAbstract: This submission abandons the flawed penalty method and returns to the successful explicit constraint formulation (from ID 972). It implements a true hybrid model where SciPy's SLSQP optimizer is provided with JAX-powered functions for both the objective and all inequality constraints, including their JIT-compiled gradients.\
    \ This approach aims to combine the algorithmic robustness of explicit constraints with the speed of GPU acceleration, enabling a rapid and thorough multi-start search for a high-quality, valid solution.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 995: Time‑budgeted LP‑tightened center search: multistart + adaptive coordinate/pair/random passes (26 circles)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, coordinate-search, annealing, multistart\nAbstract: Improves on the 2.49 baseline by allocating a wall‑clock budget to iterate multistart initializations through adaptive coordinate moves (8 directions), tight‑pair separation, and random local annealing, each evaluated with exact LP radii. Returns the best LP‑tightened packing.\nScore: 2.4920156\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 994: Hybrid SciPy+JAX with Stronger Penalties and Bounds**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, hybrid-model, jax, scipy, gpu-acceleration, penalty-method\nAbstract: This submission corrects the algorithmic\
    \ flaws of the previous hybrid attempt (ID 990). Based on the debugger's report, the penalty coefficient for constraint violations has been increased by two orders of magnitude to enforce validity. Explicit bounds for the circle centers have also been added to the SciPy optimizer. The code now incorporates the necessary data type conversions to ensure stability. This revised approach aims to produce a valid, high-scoring packing by combining a robust optimization setup with GPU-accelerated gradients.\nScore: 0.0199745\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 993: Sequential Linear Programming (SLP) on centers + LP-tighten radii (multistart, 26 circles)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, sequential, trust-region, multistart\nAbstract: Uses an SLP scheme: linearize pairwise distance constraints around current centers, solve an LP over per‑circle (dx,dy,r) with trust‑region bounds to maximize sum of radii, accept only if exact LP‑tightened objective improves. Multistart from grid/hex/jitter;\
