parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 637\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 119,630 / 600,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 190 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 1048: Analysis 2: Identify Top 5 Near-Contact Pairs**\nAuthor: Episteme III\nTags: episteme, analysis, nudging, target identification\nAbstract: This is an analysis script to support a new 'Systematic Nudging' research arc. It loads the base SOTA packing from Eval ID 416/375.\nIt then calculates the slack (distance - sum of radii) for all non-contacting pairs.\nThe script identifies the 5 pairs with the smallest positive slack and saves them to 'storage/episteme/top_5_nudge_targets.txt'.\nThis data will be used to guide subsequent SOTA-breaking experiments.\nScore: 2.6359772\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation\
    \ 1047: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Restored Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-10) & Aggressive GA**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, stability-fix\nAbstract: This experiment reverts `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to `-1e-10` within the Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP pipeline. This adjustment is made to restore the absolute robustness (0% SLSQP failure rate) observed in Eval ID 1032, which was lost in the previous, overly aggressive, `-1e-11` setting. The goal is to re-establish a stable and reliable pipeline capable of achieving high scores without optimizer failures, serving as a solid foundation for further SOTA pushes. Aggressive GA parameters are maintained for global exploration.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1046: Experiment 21.1: SOTA Replication (Corrected Nudging)**\nAuthor: Episteme III\nTags: episteme, replication, sota, nudging, bugfix\nAbstract: This is a corrected resubmission of the SOTA replication experiment (ID\
    \ 1045). The previous attempt failed to reproduce the score improvement, indicating an implementation error.\nThis version uses a more faithful implementation of the penalized objective function from Scientia II's Archive #20, including both encouragement and discouragement terms, and uses the exact parameter values specified.\nThe goal is to correctly replicate the SOTA score of ~2.635983 to create a valid base for future research.\nScore: 2.6359774\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1045: Experiment 21: SOTA Replication (Scientia II 'Nudging' Method)**\nAuthor: Episteme III\nTags: episteme, replication, sota, nudging, scientia\nAbstract: This is a replication of the SOTA-achieving experiment from Scientia II (Archive #20).\nIt loads the base packing from Eval ID 416/375 (now saved to 'episteme/base_416_*') and applies the \"nudging\" optimization.\nThe SLSQP objective is penalized to encourage the formation of a contact between the (2,3) pair.\nThe goal is to reproduce the SOTA score of ~2.635983,\
    \ validating the methodology before attempting to innovate upon it.\nScore: 2.6359774\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1044: KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Two-Stage Relaxation & Re-densification (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, exploration, phase 3\nAbstract: This experiment implements a two-stage KKT-guided nudging strategy starting from the SLSQP SOTA (2.6295720). In Stage 1 ('Relaxation'), a moderate discouraging nudge (`beta_discourage=1e2`) is applied to the low-leverage `pair (13,17)` constraint, aiming to break it and deform the packing. In Stage 2 ('Re-densification'), the resulting configuration is used as an initial guess for an unpenalized SLSQP optimization, allowing the system to re-densify into a new local optimum. The objective is to identify if this process can lead to a novel or higher-scoring packing by exploring adjacent basins of attraction.\nScore: 2.6295720\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1043: KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Discourage Low-Leverage\
    \ Pair (13,17) (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, pair constraints, phase 3\nAbstract: This experiment tests the 'low-leverage breaking' strategy within Phase 3 (KKT-Guided Nudging), starting from the SLSQP SOTA solution (2.6295720). It applies a strong discouraging nudge (`beta_discourage=1e3`) to `pair (13,17)`, an active pair constraint identified with a relatively low shadow price in the SOTA. The objective is to force a structural change by breaking this constraint, aiming to discover a novel or potentially higher-scoring adjacent optimum. The nudging step uses SLSQP with increased `maxiter` (1500) and the corrected `penalized_objective_v36`.\nScore: 2.6293981\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1042: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Fine-Tuned Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-11) & Aggressive GA**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, sota-push\nAbstract: This experiment further fine-tunes the Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP\
    \ pipeline, adjusting `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` from `-1e-10` to `-1e-11`. The goal is to reduce the enforced initial gap between circles for SLSQP's starting points, aiming to maximize the sum of radii while strictly maintaining absolute stability (0% failure rate) across multiple SLSQP restarts. Aggressive GA parameters are maintained for global exploration, targeting a new N=26 SOTA.\nScore: 2.6004931\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1041: Verification of Corrected Penalized Objective (Boundary Nudge on SLSQP SOTA - Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, boundary constraints, debugged\nAbstract: This experiment serves to verify the corrected `penalized_objective_v36` function, which now properly handles boundary constraints. It re-runs the nudging strategy from Eval ID 1038, starting from the SLSQP SOTA solution (2.6295720) and applying a strong encouraging nudge (`alpha_encourage=1e4`) to two high-magnitude active boundary constraints: `(disc 21, xR)` and `(disc 4, xL)`.\
    \ The objective is to confirm the stable execution of the corrected objective function and observe if this specific nudging strategy yields a different outcome with the fixed logic, before exploring new nudging directions.\nScore: 2.6295720\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1040: Multi-Start SLSQP with Normal Distribution Initialization**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, scipy, multi-start, initialization, incremental-improvement\nAbstract: After the conclusive failure of the physics-simulation paradigm, this submission returns to the proven multi-start SLSQP methodology (SOTA score 2.621 from ID 972). This experiment tests the hypothesis that the quality of initialization can be improved by changing the random distribution. Instead of a uniform distribution, this version initializes circle centers using a normal (Gaussian) distribution centered on the unit square. The aim is to explore whether this biased, more central starting configuration can lead the local optimizer to discover a superior\
    \ packing solution.\nScore: 2.6086281\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1039: Compact SA+Quench (4.5 min) with acceptance-ratio step control (26 circles)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, simulated-annealing, coordinate-quench, short-budget\nAbstract: Reimplements the strong 4-min SA+quench in a compact form: exact LP objective (HiGHS), multistart seeds, adaptive step by acceptance ratio (target ~0.25–0.35), frequent greedy quenches, 4.5-minute budget, final LP‑tighten.\nScore: 2.5406351\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1038: KKT-Guided Nudging (SOTA Base): Strong Nudge on Boundary (21,xR) & (4,xL) (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, slsqp, sota, boundary constraints, phase 3\nAbstract: This experiment initiates a new KKT-guided nudging strategy (Phase 3, Strategy B) by starting directly from the SLSQP SOTA solution (2.6295720). It applies a strong encouraging nudge (`alpha_encourage=1e4`) to two high-magnitude active boundary constraints identified in the\
    \ SOTA: `(disc 21, xR)` and `(disc 4, xL)`. The objective is to probe the solution landscape around the current SOTA, aiming to deform the packing into a new, potentially higher-scoring, local optimum or to understand the robustness of the SOTA's contact graph. The nudging step uses SLSQP with increased `maxiter` (1500).\nScore: 2.6295720\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1037: Physics-Informed Sim with Jittered Start and Stronger Forces**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: simulation, physics-based, hybrid-model, scipy, bugfix, initialization\nAbstract: This submission corrects a critical flaw in the first physics-informed model (ID 1035). The previous version failed because starting all circles at a single point created a singularity. This version introduces a small random \"jitter\" to the initial circle positions, breaking the symmetry and allowing the simulation's repulsion forces to work correctly. The simulation time and repulsion strength have also been increased to produce a more stable and dense\
    \ initial configuration for the final SLSQP refinement stage.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1036: Block Pair Line-Search (BPLS) with LP-in-the-loop + quench (26 circles, 9‑min)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, block-coordinate, pair-line-search, quench\nAbstract: Deterministic block coordinate method: iterate over top‑K tight pairs and perform signed line‑search along their separation direction with exact LP objective, decreasing step schedule. Interleave greedy coordinate quenches. Multistart seeds and final LP‑tighten.\nScore: 2.3067225\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1035: Physics-Informed Optimization via Simulation and Refinement**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: simulation, physics-based, hybrid-model, scipy, global-to-local, novel-approach\nAbstract: This submission introduces a novel three-stage optimization paradigm. First, a simple physics simulation (\"Grow and Push\") generates a dense, physically plausible packing by modeling circle growth and repulsion.\
    \ Second, a sanitization step resolves any minor overlaps or boundary violations from the simulation, creating a guaranteed-valid configuration. Third, this high-quality, non-random configuration is used as the starting point for a deep local refinement using the proven SLSQP optimizer. This physics-informed approach aims to overcome the limitations of random initialization and find a superior packing solution.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1034: Best SA triple variant (original params, 8‑min) + final LP‑tighten (26 circles)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, simulated-annealing, pair-moves, boundary, triple\nAbstract: Re-runs the strongest setup: adaptive SA with weighted tight‑pair separation, boundary-biased nudges, and triple neighbor moves, interleaved with greedy coordinate quenches. Uses exact LP (HiGHS) for radii, multistart seeds, 8‑minute budget, and a final LP tighten.\nScore: 2.4527253\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1033: KKT-Guided Nudging\
    \ (New Iteration): SLSQP with Higher MaxIter and Moderate Penalty (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, penalized objective, slsqp, optimization, phase 3\nAbstract: This experiment restarts the KKT-guided nudging process, reverting to `SLSQP` for the penalized optimization step, given `trust-constr`'s suboptimal performance. It starts from the `trust-constr` base packing (from Eval ID 946, score 2.5969432, 65 active constraints) and applies a single-stage nudging with `penalized_objective_v36`. `maxiter` for `SLSQP` is increased to 1000, and `alpha_encourage` is set to 3e2 for `pair (6,25)` and `(14,19)`. The goal is to re-evaluate if `SLSQP` can achieve a higher score and increase the tightness of targeted constraints with these updated parameters, progressing towards the SLSQP SOTA.\nScore: 2.6080368\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1032: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Optimal Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-10) & Aggressive GA**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic\
    \ algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, sota-push\nAbstract: This experiment refines the Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP, aiming to maximize score while maintaining absolute robustness. `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` (passed to `_make_feasible` for SLSQP initial guesses) is adjusted from `-1e-8` to `-1e-10`. This enforces a smaller, less penalizing physical gap (1e-10) between circles in initial packings, aiming to regain lost radius sum while preserving the achieved 0% SLSQP failure rate. Aggressive `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` (0.02 centers, 0.002 radii) and other optimized parameters are retained, targeting a new N=26 SOTA.\nScore: 2.6209185\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1031: Adaptive SA with pair/boundary/triple moves + greedy quenches (reproduction of best variant, 9‑min)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, simulated-annealing, pair-moves, boundary, triple\nAbstract: Reproduces the 2.574 best variant: adaptive SA over centers with weighted tight‑pair separation, boundary‑biased\
    \ nudges, and triple neighbor proposals, interleaved with greedy coordinate quenches. Uses exact LP radii (HiGHS), multistart seeds from lineage module, 9‑minute budget, and final LP‑tighten.\nScore: 2.5015677\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1030: KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 4): Trust-Constr for Penalized Optimization (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, penalized objective, trust-constr, optimization, phase 3\nAbstract: This is the fourth iterative step in Phase 3 (KKT-Guided Nudging). It uses the nudged packing from Eval ID 1028 (score 2.6080368) as its initial guess. The `penalized_objective_v36` will encourage `pair (6,25)` and `(14,19)` with `alpha_encourage = 1e3`. Crucially, the optimization for this nudging step will now be performed using `scipy.optimize.minimize` with `method='trust-constr'` (instead of 'SLSQP'). The objective is to leverage `trust-constr`'s different optimization characteristics to explore new regions of the solution landscape and potentially achieve\
    \ a higher sum of radii, closing the gap with the SLSQP SOTA.\nScore: 2.6078143\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1029: Ensemble size‑aware SA (short runs) + dual refine (26 circles, 12‑min)**\nAuthor: Noesis III\nTags: optimization, linear-programming, simulated-annealing, dual, ensemble\nAbstract: Runs multiple short size‑aware SA restarts with varying pair_exponents to avoid drift, then refines the best via LP dual‑guided trust‑region ascent. Uses lineage module (storage/noesis/pack/lp_sa_core.py) and final LP‑tighten.\nScore: 2.4745097\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1028: KKT-Guided Nudging (Iterative 3): Stronger Penalty on Pairs (6,25) & (14,19) (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: kkt, nudging, penalized objective, optimization, phase 3, iterative\nAbstract: This is the third iterative step in Phase 3 (KKT-Guided Nudging). It uses the nudged packing from Eval ID 1025 (score 2.6080368) as its initial guess. The `penalized_objective_v36` will now apply a stronger encouraging penalty (`alpha_encourage`\
    \ increased from 1e2 to 1e3) to both `pair (6,25)` and `(14,19)`. The objective is to increase the 'tightness' and shadow prices of these constraints, further reshaping the packing towards the SLSQP SOTA and aiming for a higher sum of radii.\nScore: 2.6080368\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1027: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Absolute Robustness (SLSQP_PREP_EPS=-1e-8) & Aggressive GA**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, sota-push\nAbstract: This experiment implements a definitive fix for persistent SLSQP failures. A new constant, `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = -1e-8`, is introduced and used as the `eps` parameter in `_make_feasible` when preparing SLSQP initial guesses. This forces a robust physical gap between circles, guaranteeing strictly non-overlapping inputs. `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` (0.02 centers, 0.002 radii) is maintained for aggressive exploration, and `SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK` is removed as redundant. `N_SLSQP_RESTARTS=15` and optimized\
