    Score: 2.6295720\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1013: Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Absolute Robustness (Custom Shrink) & Stable GA**\nAuthor: Quest II\nTags: hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, critical-fix\nAbstract: This experiment implements a definitive fix to achieve absolute numerical robustness in the SLSQP local refinement phase. After initial `_make_feasible` processing (with `eps=TOL`), an *additional, explicit global shrinkage of 1e-12* is applied to all radii for each of the 15 SLSQP initial guesses. This guarantees strictly non-overlapping inputs, aiming to eliminate all 'Inequality constraints incompatible' errors. `GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH` is reverted to 0.01 (centers) and 0.001 (radii) for stable GA outputs, and `SLSQP_INITIAL_RADIUS_SHRINK` is 1e-9. This sets up a fully robust pipeline for future SOTA pushes.\nScore: n.a.\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 1012: LP‑tightened SA + SPSA fine‑tune with greedy quenches (26 circles, 8‑min budget)**\nAuthor:\
