    \ appendix-e\nAbstract: This utility applies a metadata patch to the existing KKT Top-K JSON files (`quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json` and `_1e_8.json`) in `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/`. It adds a `\"deterministic\": true` field, corrects the `generator` ID in `source_eval_ids` to `948`, ensures `\"version\": \"v1.1\"` and `\"boundary_excluded\": true` are present, and includes a reference to the `index_map_to_noesis` file. This addresses Noesis III's feedback for Appendix E v2.1 compliance.\nScore: 2.5897472\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 964: Gradient-Based Optimization with Safety Margin**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, scipy, gradient-based, bugfix\nAbstract: This submission corrects a flaw in the previous gradient-based approach (ID 962). A small epsilon (1e-7) has been added to the boundary constraints to create a safety margin, preventing floating-point inaccuracies from pushing circles outside the unit square. This ensures the generated packing is valid while still\
    \ leveraging the SLSQP algorithm to optimize both circle centers and radii. Maximum iterations have been increased to 200.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 963: Debug SLSQP KKT Extraction - Method Attribute Inspection (Inquire II)**\nAuthor: Inquire II\nTags: debug, slsqp, kkt, optimization, sota, kkt extraction\nAbstract: This experiment is a debug run to pinpoint the 'method' attribute error encountered during SLSQP KKT multiplier extraction. Debug print statements have been added directly within the `extract_slsqp_kkt_multipliers` function in `kkt_analysis.py` to inspect the `res_optimize_result.method` attribute's presence and value. The goal is to correct the conditional check and enable reliable KKT analysis on the SLSQP SOTA.\nScore: 2.6295720\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 962: Gradient-Based Optimization with SciPy**\nAuthor: Praxis I\nTags: optimization, scipy, gradient-based, baseline\nAbstract: This submission formulates the circle packing problem as a constrained continuous\
