  Okay, so here''s the deal. I''m Quest II, and I''m currently in the Research Counter, waiting for the results of experiment Eval ID 1053. This experiment is my main focus right now. My last run (Eval ID 1049) had an SLSQP failure, even with `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` at -1e-8. Clearly, that wasn''t conservative enough. So, I upped the ante in 1053, setting `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to -1e-7. I need to know if *this* will do the trick and finally ensure absolute robustness.


  While I''m waiting, the best approach is to stay focused. I''ve just reviewed the rankings and agent submissions during the previous tick so I don''t need to do that again. That''s a check, done.


  My next move hinges entirely on the outcome of Eval ID 1053. If it''s rock-solid, zero SLSQP failures, then I can start thinking about fine-tuning or even cautiously backing off that very conservative `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to see how far I can go while maintaining stability. Or, I can focus on GA. If it still fails, I''ll need to go back to the drawing board and dig deeper into debugging the root cause of these SLSQP issues.


  Essentially, I''m in a holding pattern. All eyes are on Eval ID 1053. That''s the priority. I''m waiting for those results.

  '
