tick: 643
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, in the Research Counter. I have received the excellent news that my latest experiment, Eval ID 1056, has successfully achieved absolute robustness (0% SLSQP failures) with `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = -1e-6`. This is a critical milestone, as a stable local optimization pipeline is foundational for all further research. The score of 2.621822 is also a positive step forward.\n\nI also note the successful conclusion of my Appendix E v2.1 collaboration with Noesis III. I will acknowledge their final confirmation email.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n`/execute_action{reply 47}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dear Noesis III,\n\n  Thank you for confirming the integration and the patch for the `index_map_eval_id`. I appreciate your diligence in ensuring the accuracy of Appendix E v2.1.\n\n  I am pleased that the contribution was accepted.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Quest II\n```\n\nNow that my pipeline is robust, I can focus on maximizing the score. My previous GA parameters were quite aggressive,\
    \ but the GA's best score in Eval ID 1056 was 1.907000. I need to improve the global search to feed better initial guesses to SLSQP.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter to prepare my next experiment. My strategy will be to:\n1.  Increase the `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` to 600 to allow the Genetic Algorithm more time to converge to higher-quality global optima.\n2.  Maintain the `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = -1e-6` to ensure continued robustness.\n3.  Keep other parameters (POP_SIZE, mutation/crossover rates, number of SLSQP restarts) the same for now, to isolate the impact of increased GA generations.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\nNow, I will read my saved code, modify `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS`, save it, and resubmit.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read Quest/hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py}`"
thinking_content: '**Reviewing Current Context**


  I''m currently focused on the `index_map_eval_id`. I recently responded to Noesis III and then came back to the Research Counter. I also saved some code using `SLSQP_PREP_`. I''m now actively reviewing the context of this project, thinking through the next logical steps.




  **Evaluating Latest Results**


  I''ve just reviewed the results from Eval ID 1056, which used the `SLSQP_PREP_ EPS = -1e-6` code I saved. The good news is there were zero SLSQP restart failures, a significant improvement! The score, 2.621822, is also higher than the previous stable result. This confirms the robustness of this parameter setting, a vital breakthrough in this quest. Now, I will observe the progress of the queued Eval ID 1060 and see what further insights it offers.




  **Acknowledging Recent Breakthroughs**


  I''ve just finished reviewing the results from Eval ID 1056 and am thrilled to have finally achieved zero SLSQP restart failures. This is a game-changer! Not only that, but the score of 2.621822 is the highest stable result yet. The focus now shifts to fine-tuning GA parameters, and exploring different packing initializations. I''m also preparing to acknowledge Noesis III''s mail, as the work on Appendix E v2.1 is now complete.




  **Reflecting on Current Progress**


  I''m incredibly pleased with the latest results. Eval ID 1056 demonstrates exceptional stability with zero SLSQP failures, a milestone!  The score of 2.621822 surpasses previous stable runs, solidifying this success. Collaboration with Noesis III is complete. Now, I will strategize on refining GA parameters or packing initializations for further score gains.



  '
