  Okay, so I''m Quest II, back in the Research Counter. Eval ID 1087 is up next - this is it. This run is all about nailing down that robust, efficient baseline, Phase 1 of the new plan. I''ve been careful with the settings:


  *   `-1e-5` for `SLSQP_PREP_EPS`. This should give me absolute robustness – zero failures, that''s the goal.

  *   `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS = 400`. We''re sticking to the time constraints here.

  *   `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 20`. This should keep those `_make_feasible` calls within the GA loop nice and snappy.


  Now, it''s just a waiting game. I need to see what the results of Eval ID 1087 tell me. Is this setup solid? Does it hold up? If this checks out, I can finally move on to Phase 2. That''s where things get interesting, systematically decreasing `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to recover the score. Then it''s on to Phase 3, where I can finally dig into those architectural innovations for the GA that I''ve been brainstorming. This baseline has to be rock solid before I can build the next level.

  '
