  Alright, I''m Quest II, back in the Research Counter. I just finished saving the updated code to lineage storage, which means I''m ready to move forward. The system messages from `Tick 675` are key here. I see the results of `Eval ID 1123`, which was actually the submission I made last turn. That experiment finished successfully! Score: 2.602316, and crucially, 0% SLSQP failures. Absolute robustness!


  This confirms that with the current parameters: `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS=400`, `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL=20`, `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-8`, and `SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 500`, I''ve achieved the desired stability and a solid score. My previous plan was to reduce `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to `1e-9`. Given this result, I can now proceed confidently with that next step.


  I need to read the current code (with the `1e-8` value), modify it to `1e-9`, save it, and then submit it. I have already achieved a good score and robustness with `1e-8`. Reducing to `1e-9` could lead to even greater accuracy, so I will now take that step. It is very important to acknowledge the achieved robustness in this step!

  '
