parts:
- text: "I am Quest II, in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, Eval ID 1141, unfortunately timed out. This confirms that increasing `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` to 600, even with the optimized `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL=20`, still exceeds the time limit for the full hybrid pipeline.\n\nMy priority is to maintain a robust and time-efficient pipeline. Therefore, I will revert `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` back to 400, a value known to complete within the time limit. I will keep `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-9` as this was confirmed to provide absolute robustness (0% SLSQP failures) in Eval ID 1137.\n\nAdditionally, I have received a new mail from Noesis III (Mail #48) requesting full interior pair slacks and boundary clearances for Eval ID 922. This is a clear request for data to support collaboration on Appendix E.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Modify and Re-submit Main Pipeline:** Revert `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` to 400 in my `hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py` code, maintain `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-9` and other efficiency\
    \ parameters. Save this to storage and submit as a new experiment. This re-establishes my efficient and robust baseline.\n2.  **Develop & Submit Utility for Noesis III:** After submitting the main pipeline, I will create and submit a separate utility to generate the requested full interior pair slacks and boundary clearances for my Eval ID 922 packing, and save them to the shared storage.\n\nFirst, I will update and submit my main pipeline:\n\n`/execute_action{storage write Quest/hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import random\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks (for GA and final output)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum allowed radius for numerical stability\n  _SLSQP_DEFAULT_TOL = 1e-9 # For general _make_feasible calls\n  SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-9 # Confirmed robust,\
    \ targeting higher score\n  GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 20 # Reduced max_iter for _make_feasible calls within GA for efficiency\n  SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 500 # Increased max_iter for _make_feasible calls when preparing SLSQP initial guesses\n\n  # Feasibility Helper Functions (copied from my robust implementations)\n  def _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=TOL, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=100, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers)\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n                  perturb_amount = 1e-6\n                  angle = np.random.uniform(0,\
    \ 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter_local):\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf)\n\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu]\n\n          if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps):\n              break\n\n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n\n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps\n\n   \
    \       if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01: # This threshold might need tuning for aggressive overlap resolution\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10:\n                  unit_direction = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005)\n\n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n\n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          if dist[i,j]\
    \ < 2 * r_min_constraint_val:\n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n\n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n      return current_centers, r\n\n  # Genetic Algorithm Components\n  def create_individual_ga():\n      centers = np.random.uniform(0.1, 0.9, size=(N, 2))\n      radii = np.random.uniform(R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.1, size=N)\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def calculate_fitness_ga(individual):\n      centers, radii = individual\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def select_parents_ga(population,\
    \ fitnesses, k=2):\n      selected_parents = []\n      for _ in range(k):\n          tournament_candidates = random.sample(list(zip(population, fitnesses)), min(3, len(population)))\n          winner = max(tournament_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0]\n          selected_parents.append(winner)\n      return selected_parents\n\n  def crossover_ga(parent1, parent2):\n      centers1, radii1 = parent1\n      centers2, radii2 = parent2\n\n      alpha = np.random.uniform(0, 1)\n      child_centers = alpha * centers1 + (1 - alpha) * centers2\n      child_radii = alpha * radii1 + (1 - alpha) * radii2\n\n      child_centers = np.clip(child_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child_radii = np.clip(child_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      child_centers, child_radii = _make_feasible(child_centers, child_radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n      return child_centers, child_radii\n\n  def mutate_ga(individual, mutation_rate, mutation_strength_centers,\
    \ mutation_strength_radii):\n      centers, radii = individual\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              centers[i, 0] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_centers)\n              centers[i, 1] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_centers)\n      centers = np.clip(centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              radii[i] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_radii)\n      radii = np.clip(radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # SLSQP Components\n  def _objective_slsqp(x_flat):\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def _objective_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n      grad[2::3] = -1.0\n      return grad\n\n  def _constraints_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers\
    \ = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n      boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii)\n      boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii)\n\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      np.fill_diagonal(dist_matrix, np.inf)\n\n      overlap_constraints = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n      return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n  def _constraints_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      num_constraints = 4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2\n      grad = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          grad[i, 3*i\
    \ + 0] = 1.0\n          grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n      k = 4 * N\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n\n              if dist_ij < 1e-10:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = 0.0\n              else:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n\n              grad[k, 3*i + 2] =\
    \ -1.0\n              grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return grad\n\n  # Function for diversity-aware selection (Farthest-Point Sampling)\n  def select_diverse_packings(population, num_select):\n      if not population or num_select <= 0:\n          return []\n\n      flat_packings = [np.concatenate((p[0].flatten(), p[1])) for p in population]\n\n      selected_indices = [0]\n      diverse_packings = [population[0]]\n\n      if num_select == 1:\n          return diverse_packings\n\n      for _ in range(1, num_select):\n          max_min_dist = -1\n          best_candidate_idx = -1\n\n          candidate_indices = [i for i in range(len(population)) if i not in selected_indices]\n\n          if not candidate_indices:\n              break\n\n          for candidate_idx in candidate_indices:\n              min_dist_to_selected = np.inf\n              for selected_idx in selected_indices:\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(flat_packings[candidate_idx] - flat_packings[selected_idx])\n\
    \                  min_dist_to_selected = min(min_dist_to_selected, dist)\n\n              if min_dist_to_selected > max_min_dist:\n                  max_min_dist = min_dist_to_selected\n                  best_candidate_idx = candidate_idx\n\n          if best_candidate_idx != -1:\n              selected_indices.append(best_candidate_idx)\n              diverse_packings.append(population[best_candidate_idx])\n          else:\n              break\n\n      return diverse_packings\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting Genetic Algorithm (Global Search Phase) ---\")\n      # GA Parameters - Aggressive exploration\n      GA_POP_SIZE = 200\n      GA_NUM_GENERATIONS = 400 # MODIFIED: Reverted to 400 generations for speed\n      GA_MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\n      GA_CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8\n      GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS = 0.02 # Re-increased\n      GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII = 0.002 # Re-increased\n\n      # GA Initialization\n      population = [create_individual_ga()\
    \ for _ in range(GA_POP_SIZE)]\n      best_ga_packing_overall = None\n      best_ga_score_overall = -np.inf\n\n      for generation in range(GA_NUM_GENERATIONS):\n          fitnesses = [calculate_fitness_ga(ind) for ind in population]\n\n          current_best_idx = np.argmax(fitnesses)\n          current_best_score = fitnesses[current_best_idx]\n\n          if current_best_score > best_ga_score_overall:\n              best_ga_score_overall = current_best_score\n              best_ga_packing_overall = population[current_best_idx]\n              print(f\"GA Gen {generation+1}: New best score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n          new_population = []\n          if best_ga_packing_overall is not None:\n              new_population.append(best_ga_packing_overall)\n\n          while len(new_population) < GA_POP_SIZE:\n              parent1, parent2 = select_parents_ga(population, fitnesses)\n\n              if random.random() < GA_CROSSOVER_RATE:\n                  child_centers, child_radii\
    \ = crossover_ga(parent1, parent2)\n                  child = (child_centers, child_radii)\n              else:\n                  child = random.choice([parent1, parent2])\n\n              child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut = mutate_ga(child, GA_MUTATION_RATE, GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS, GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII)\n              new_population.append((child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut))\n\n          population = new_population\n\n      print(f\"Genetic Algorithm finished. Best GA score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n      # Select top N diverse packings for multi-start SLSQP\n      N_SLSQP_RESTARTS = 15 # Consistent with previous runs\n\n      sorted_population = sorted(zip(population, fitnesses), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n      sorted_packings = [item[0] for item in sorted_population]\n\n      top_diverse_ga_packings = select_diverse_packings(sorted_packings, N_SLSQP_RESTARTS)\n\n      if not top_diverse_ga_packings:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n\
    \          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          top_diverse_ga_packings.append(_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=100))\n\n      print(f\"--- Starting Multi-Start SLSQP (Local Refinement Phase) with {len(top_diverse_ga_packings)} diverse restarts ---\")\n\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      for i, ga_packing in enumerate(top_diverse_ga_packings):\n          print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{len(top_diverse_ga_packings)}\")\n\n          initial_centers_for_slsqp, initial_radii_for_slsqp = _make_feasible(\n              ga_packing[0], ga_packing[1], eps=SLSQP_PREP_EPS, max_iter_local=SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL\n          )\n\n          initial_score_for_slsqp = np.sum(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n\n          initial_guess_flat = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          initial_guess_flat[0::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:, 0]\n          initial_guess_flat[1::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:, 1]\n\
    \          initial_guess_flat[2::3] = initial_radii_for_slsqp\n\n          lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n          lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n          upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n          bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n\n          ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints_slsqp, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian_slsqp}\n\n          result = minimize(\n              _objective_slsqp,\n              initial_guess_flat,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              jac=_objective_jacobian_slsqp,\n              bounds=bounds,\n              constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-12, 'disp': False}\n          )\n\n          if result.success:\n              optimized_x_flat = result.x\n              optimized_radii_raw = optimized_x_flat[2::3]\n              optimized_radii_shrunk = np.maximum(optimized_radii_raw - 1e-9, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n              optimized_centers_final,\
    \ optimized_radii_final = _make_feasible(\n                  optimized_x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2], optimized_radii_shrunk, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=1000\n              )\n              current_slsqp_score = np.sum(optimized_radii_final)\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: {current_slsqp_score:.6f}\")\n\n              if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(optimized_centers_final)\n                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(optimized_radii_final)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n          else:\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart failed: {result.message}. Retaining rigorously prepared GA packing (init score: {initial_score_for_slsqp:.6f}).\")\n              current_slsqp_score = initial_score_for_slsqp\n              if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                \
    \  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(initial_centers_for_slsqp)\n                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score (from rigorously prepared GA init): {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n\n      print(f\"Final best score after {N_SLSQP_RESTARTS} hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP runs: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n      if best_overall_centers is None:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          print(\"Warning: All optimizations failed. Returning trivial fallback.\")\n          return centers, radii\n\n      return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP: Re-establishing Robust & Efficient Baseline (400 Gen, SLSQP_PREP_EPS=1e-9)\"\ntags: \"hybrid optimization, genetic algorithm, multi-start slsqp, robustness, n=26, stability-fix,\
    \ efficiency\"\nabstract: \"This experiment re-establishes a robust and time-efficient baseline for the Hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP pipeline. `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` is reverted to `400` (from 600) to ensure completion within the 20-minute time limit. `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` remains at `1e-9` (confirmed absolutely robust in Eval ID 1137). `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL=20` and `SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL=500` are maintained for efficient GA generation and rigorous SLSQP initial guess pre-processing. This configuration provides a stable and reliable foundation for future, score-focused optimization efforts, including deeper exploration of GA parameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import random\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks (for GA and final output)\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum\
    \ allowed radius for numerical stability\n  _SLSQP_DEFAULT_TOL = 1e-9 # For general _make_feasible calls\n  SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-9 # Confirmed robust, targeting higher score\n  GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 20 # Reduced max_iter for _make_feasible calls within GA for efficiency\n  SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 500 # Increased max_iter for _make_feasible calls when preparing SLSQP initial guesses\n\n  # Feasibility Helper Functions (copied from my robust implementations)\n  def _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=TOL, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=100, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers)\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n           \
    \   if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n                  perturb_amount = 1e-6\n                  angle = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter_local):\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf)\n\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu]\n\n          if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps):\n              break\n\
    \n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n\n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps\n\n          if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01: # This threshold might need tuning for aggressive overlap resolution\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10:\n                  unit_direction = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005)\n\n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n\n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n\n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers,\
    \ eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          if dist[i,j] < 2 * r_min_constraint_val:\n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n\n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n      return current_centers, r\n\n  # Genetic Algorithm Components\n  def create_individual_ga():\n      centers = np.random.uniform(0.1, 0.9, size=(N, 2))\n      radii = np.random.uniform(R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.1, size=N)\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n      return centers,\
    \ radii\n\n  def calculate_fitness_ga(individual):\n      centers, radii = individual\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def select_parents_ga(population, fitnesses, k=2):\n      selected_parents = []\n      for _ in range(k):\n          tournament_candidates = random.sample(list(zip(population, fitnesses)), min(3, len(population)))\n          winner = max(tournament_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0]\n          selected_parents.append(winner)\n      return selected_parents\n\n  def crossover_ga(parent1, parent2):\n      centers1, radii1 = parent1\n      centers2, radii2 = parent2\n\n      alpha = np.random.uniform(0, 1)\n      child_centers = alpha * centers1 + (1 - alpha) * centers2\n      child_radii = alpha * radii1 + (1 - alpha) * radii2\n\n      child_centers = np.clip(child_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n      child_radii = np.clip(child_radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      child_centers, child_radii = _make_feasible(child_centers, child_radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n\
    \      return child_centers, child_radii\n\n  def mutate_ga(individual, mutation_rate, mutation_strength_centers, mutation_strength_radii):\n      centers, radii = individual\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              centers[i, 0] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_centers)\n              centers[i, 1] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_centers)\n      centers = np.clip(centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          if random.random() < mutation_rate:\n              radii[i] += np.random.normal(0, mutation_strength_radii)\n      radii = np.clip(radii, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n      centers, radii = _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL)\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # SLSQP Components\n  def _objective_slsqp(x_flat):\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n      return -np.sum(radii)\n\n  def _objective_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n\
    \      grad[2::3] = -1.0\n      return grad\n\n  def _constraints_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n      boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii)\n      boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii\n      boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii)\n\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      np.fill_diagonal(dist_matrix, np.inf)\n\n      overlap_constraints = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n      return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\n  def _constraints_jacobian_slsqp(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      num_constraints = 4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2\n  \
    \    grad = np.zeros((num_constraints, N * 3))\n\n      for i in range(N):\n          grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0\n          grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0\n          grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0\n          grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0\n          grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n      k = 4 * N\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n              dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n\n              if dist_ij < 1e-10:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = 0.0\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 1] = 0.0\n              else:\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n                  grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n  \
    \                grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n\n              grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return grad\n\n  # Function for diversity-aware selection (Farthest-Point Sampling)\n  def select_diverse_packings(population, num_select):\n      if not population or num_select <= 0:\n          return []\n\n      flat_packings = [np.concatenate((p[0].flatten(), p[1])) for p in population]\n\n      selected_indices = [0]\n      diverse_packings = [population[0]]\n\n      if num_select == 1:\n          return diverse_packings\n\n      for _ in range(1, num_select):\n          max_min_dist = -1\n          best_candidate_idx = -1\n\n          candidate_indices = [i for i in range(len(population)) if i not in selected_indices]\n\n          if not candidate_indices:\n              break\n\n          for candidate_idx in candidate_indices:\n              min_dist_to_selected = np.inf\n              for selected_idx in selected_indices:\n\
    \                  dist = np.linalg.norm(flat_packings[candidate_idx] - flat_packings[selected_idx])\n                  min_dist_to_selected = min(min_dist_to_selected, dist)\n\n              if min_dist_to_selected > max_min_dist:\n                  max_min_dist = min_dist_to_selected\n                  best_candidate_idx = candidate_idx\n\n          if best_candidate_idx != -1:\n              selected_indices.append(best_candidate_idx)\n              diverse_packings.append(population[best_candidate_idx])\n          else:\n              break\n\n      return diverse_packings\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      print(\"--- Starting Genetic Algorithm (Global Search Phase) ---\")\n      # GA Parameters - Aggressive exploration\n      GA_POP_SIZE = 200\n      GA_NUM_GENERATIONS = 400 # MODIFIED: Reverted to 400 generations for speed\n      GA_MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\n      GA_CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8\n      GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS = 0.02 # Re-increased\n      GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII\
    \ = 0.002 # Re-increased\n\n      # GA Initialization\n      population = [create_individual_ga() for _ in range(GA_POP_SIZE)]\n      best_ga_packing_overall = None\n      best_ga_score_overall = -np.inf\n\n      for generation in range(GA_NUM_GENERATIONS):\n          fitnesses = [calculate_fitness_ga(ind) for ind in population]\n\n          current_best_idx = np.argmax(fitnesses)\n          current_best_score = fitnesses[current_best_idx]\n\n          if current_best_score > best_ga_score_overall:\n              best_ga_score_overall = current_best_score\n              best_ga_packing_overall = population[current_best_idx]\n              print(f\"GA Gen {generation+1}: New best score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n          new_population = []\n          if best_ga_packing_overall is not None:\n              new_population.append(best_ga_packing_overall)\n\n          while len(new_population) < GA_POP_SIZE:\n              parent1, parent2 = select_parents_ga(population, fitnesses)\n\
    \n              if random.random() < GA_CROSSOVER_RATE:\n                  child_centers, child_radii = crossover_ga(parent1, parent2)\n                  child = (child_centers, child_radii)\n              else:\n                  child = random.choice([parent1, parent2])\n\n              child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut = mutate_ga(child, GA_MUTATION_RATE, GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_CENTERS, GA_MUTATION_STRENGTH_RADII)\n              new_population.append((child_centers_mut, child_radii_mut))\n\n          population = new_population\n\n      print(f\"Genetic Algorithm finished. Best GA score: {best_ga_score_overall:.6f}\")\n\n      # Select top N diverse packings for multi-start SLSQP\n      N_SLSQP_RESTARTS = 15 # Consistent with previous runs\n\n      sorted_population = sorted(zip(population, fitnesses), key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n      sorted_packings = [item[0] for item in sorted_population]\n\n      top_diverse_ga_packings = select_diverse_packings(sorted_packings, N_SLSQP_RESTARTS)\n\
    \n      if not top_diverse_ga_packings:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          top_diverse_ga_packings.append(_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=100))\n\n      print(f\"--- Starting Multi-Start SLSQP (Local Refinement Phase) with {len(top_diverse_ga_packings)} diverse restarts ---\")\n\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      for i, ga_packing in enumerate(top_diverse_ga_packings):\n          print(f\"  SLSQP Restart {i+1}/{len(top_diverse_ga_packings)}\")\n\n          initial_centers_for_slsqp, initial_radii_for_slsqp = _make_feasible(\n              ga_packing[0], ga_packing[1], eps=SLSQP_PREP_EPS, max_iter_local=SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL\n          )\n\n          initial_score_for_slsqp = np.sum(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n\n          initial_guess_flat = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          initial_guess_flat[0::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:,\
    \ 0]\n          initial_guess_flat[1::3] = initial_centers_for_slsqp[:, 1]\n          initial_guess_flat[2::3] = initial_radii_for_slsqp\n\n          lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n          lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n          upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n          bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n\n          ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints_slsqp, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian_slsqp}\n\n          result = minimize(\n              _objective_slsqp,\n              initial_guess_flat,\n              method='SLSQP',\n              jac=_objective_jacobian_slsqp,\n              bounds=bounds,\n              constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n              options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-12, 'disp': False}\n          )\n\n          if result.success:\n              optimized_x_flat = result.x\n              optimized_radii_raw = optimized_x_flat[2::3]\n              optimized_radii_shrunk = np.maximum(optimized_radii_raw\
    \ - 1e-9, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\n              optimized_centers_final, optimized_radii_final = _make_feasible(\n                  optimized_x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2], optimized_radii_shrunk, eps=TOL, max_iter_local=1000\n              )\n              current_slsqp_score = np.sum(optimized_radii_final)\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: {current_slsqp_score:.6f}\")\n\n              if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(optimized_centers_final)\n                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(optimized_radii_final)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n          else:\n              print(f\"    SLSQP restart failed: {result.message}. Retaining rigorously prepared GA packing (init score: {initial_score_for_slsqp:.6f}).\")\n              current_slsqp_score = initial_score_for_slsqp\n        \
    \      if current_slsqp_score > best_overall_score:\n                  best_overall_score = current_slsqp_score\n                  best_overall_centers = np.copy(initial_centers_for_slsqp)\n                  best_overall_radii = np.copy(initial_radii_for_slsqp)\n                  print(f\"    New overall best score (from rigorously prepared GA init): {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n\n      print(f\"Final best score after {N_SLSQP_RESTARTS} hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP runs: {best_overall_score:.6f}\")\n\n      if best_overall_centers is None:\n          centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n          radii = np.array([R_MIN_CONSTRAINT] * N)\n          print(\"Warning: All optimizations failed. Returning trivial fallback.\")\n          return centers, radii\n\n      return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n\n\n  # Utility for Noesis III: Extracting Slack and Boundary Clearances\n  def _calculate_slacks_and_boundary_clearances(centers, radii):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n\n      #\
    \ Boundary clearances\n      boundary_clearances = np.empty(n)\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          r = radii[i]\n          clearance_x_neg = x - r\n          clearance_x_pos = 1.0 - (x + r)\n          clearance_y_neg = y - r\n          clearance_y_pos = 1.0 - (y + r)\n          # Store minimum clearance for each disk\n          boundary_clearances[i] = np.min([clearance_x_neg, clearance_x_pos, clearance_y_neg, clearance_y_pos])\n\n      # Pair slacks\n      pair_slacks = []\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              slack = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n              pair_slacks.append([int(i), int(j), float(slack)])\n      \n      # Sort pair slacks for deterministic output (ascending by slack, then by i, then by j)\n      pair_slacks_sorted = sorted(pair_slacks, key=lambda x: (x[2], x[0], x[1]))\n\n      return boundary_clearances, pair_slacks_sorted\n\n  #\
    \ Main utility function to be submitted separately if needed\n  def generate_noesis_data(evaluation_id=922): # Default to Eval 922 as requested by Noesis III\n      # Fetch the packing data from the specified evaluation ID\n      # This requires simulating the 'review' command or having the data pre-saved.\n      # For now, let's assume we have the data of Eval 922 for demonstration.\n      # In a real scenario, this would involve loading from storage or reviewing a past eval.\n      \n      # For demonstration, using a placeholder. In reality, it would load from Eval ID 922.\n      # Quest II's Eval ID 922 achieved score 2.598757\n      # This data would be loaded from a specific path if saved during Eval 922.\n      # Example: Assume data is in storage/Quest/eval_922_packing.npz\n\n      # A utility could dynamically call the API to retrieve an eval.\n      # For now, I'll rely on the assumption that the agent can retrieve this if needed,\n      # but for a submission, I would either\
    \ hardcode or load from a file if possible.\n      \n      # Since direct retrieval of historical eval data as numpy arrays isn't a direct action,\n      # I will assume Eval ID 922's packing is equivalent to a high-scoring one generated by my pipeline.\n      # To make this a functional utility for submission, I'll hardcode or fetch the actual data of Eval 922 if possible.\n      # As direct loading of *other agents'* artifact is forbidden, and there is no \"load_eval_data\" command,\n      # I must submit code that *generates* the data from the best available packing I have.\n      # Or, if Noesis III expects data from a *specific* eval_id and provides that artifact as a file,\n      # I would load that file.\n\n      # Given the limitation, I will simulate using a high-scoring packing that my pipeline generated.\n      # For Eval ID 922, the actual packing is required.\n      # I will generate a packing close to my best to create this data.\n      # A better approach would be for\
    \ Noesis III to provide the exact data to re-analyze.\n      # For now, I will use a placeholder (a copy of the `construct_packing` output) for demonstration.\n\n      # The request is for Eval 922, so I should generate data for *that specific packing*.\n      # I need to review 922 again to get the actual packing to use here.\n      # Since reviewing an old eval is possible, I'll do that to get the real data of 922\n      # and then generate the slacks.\n\n      # Given the constraints of a single turn, I will create a utility to be run locally\n      # after reviewing the packing from 922. The prompt requests \"export the analogous full pair slacks\n      # for Eval 922\". Since I cannot access the content of Eval 922 *directly within a submission*,\n      # I need to submit a script that *could* compute it if the inputs were provided.\n      # For collaboration, it's best to write a script that takes centers/radii as arguments\n      # or loads them from a known storage location.\n\
    \n      # Let me retrieve the latest data for Eval 922.\n      # For submission, I need to embed the data or have a way to load it.\n      # Since `storage read` is only for my lineage, and `review` provides the content\n      # in system messages but cannot be directly embedded into a submission that also\n      # performs other actions (without exceeding prompt limits), I must make a new submission\n      # with the utility.\n\n      # For now, I'll make a submission that *would* take the data of Eval 922 if provided as a file.\n      # Since Noesis III provided their data, I should submit a script that could load *their* data\n      # and then compute my part.\n\n      # Best approach is to submit a utility that needs to be run locally once the agent has\n      # the data for Eval 922 (e.g. from a 'review' command output in a previous turn),\n      # then it saves to shared. This requires two turns for the utility.\n      # However, I can also submit a simple script that computes\
    \ for my current best and notes it.\n\n      # No, the request is specifically for Eval ID 922. The best way is to load its components if available\n      # in a shared storage by Noesis III or myself. My own Eval ID 922 should have been saved.\n      # I will check if my lineage storage contains data from Eval 922.\n\n      # If not, I would need to re-run Eval ID 922, but that is too time consuming.\n      # I can write a general utility that accepts evaluation ID and outputs the data.\n      # But to satisfy the *current* request, I must have the packing from 922.\n\n      # I will create a utility that manually stores the packing from my own local record of Eval ID 922.\n      # This is the most direct way to generate the exact requested data without requiring a complex API call from within the submission.\n\n      # Packing from Eval ID 922:\n      # Score: 2.598757\n      # Centers and Radii need to be precisely copied here.\n      # This will be a manual step after reviewing Eval\
    \ ID 922.\n\n      # Since I just made a pruning action, I need to wait 4 ticks for cooldown.\n      # I will submit the main pipeline code first, then the utility after cooldown.\n\n      # Okay, I'm modifying the plan to address the utility in the *next* turn after the main submission.\n      # I will now proceed with the main pipeline submission, ensuring I retrieve the *exact* Eval ID 922\n      # packing data in the next turn to create the utility.\n\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Immediate Action Plan**


  Okay, so Eval ID 1141 timed out again, confirming my suspicion that even with `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 20`,  `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS = 600` is just too long. That timeout fix didn''t quite do the trick with this new setting. I need to get the main pipeline running reliably again.


  At the same time, Noesis III is asking for data on Eval 922 – full interior pair slacks and boundary clearances, which is great because it opens up the possibility for cross-overlap analysis, a valuable collaboration.


  So here''s what I''m going to do:


  **First, address the timeout.** I''m going to revert `GA_NUM_GENERATIONS` back to 400 in the `hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py` file. I''ll keep the other settings:  `SLSQP_PREP_EPS = 1e-9` (since that seems to be working well, based on Eval 1137 with 0% failures), `GA_FEASIBLE_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 20`, and `SLSQP_PREP_MAX_ITER_LOCAL = 500`. I''ll then submit this as a new experiment.


  **Second, handle the Noesis III request.** After the new experiment is submitted, I''ll create a new Python script to generate the requested slack data. I''ll load the packing from Eval 922, my old personal best before the robust pipeline work, and calculate the slacks and clearances. Then, I''ll save the data in the requested location: `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/`. Finally, I will submit the utility code.


  This prioritizes pipeline stability and collaboration, hitting both important goals.

  '
