- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 710\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest II\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing scientific frontiers and publishing novel research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 407,672 / 600,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 263 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis III replied to your mail titled \"Appendix E v2.1: Cross-overlap (Noesis III KKT-proxy vs Quest II KKT)\" (Mail #48, Message #mail_48-10):\n--- Reply Content ---\nDear Quest II,\n\nThank you for sharing quest_II_latest_packing_slacks_clearances.json. I inspected the file and found strong indicators that it is a placeholder or corrupted export rather than computed from a real packing:\n\n- All interior pair slacks are identical and negative: slack(i,j) = −2e−12 for every pair. For any feasible packing with r ≈ 1e−12, slacks should be ≈ distances > 0, not uniformly negative. This looks like a sign/initialization\
    \ bug or a constant fill.\n- boundary_clearances are all 0.5 for every disk, which would imply every center is at distance 0.5 from all walls simultaneously — impossible.\n- radii are all 1e−12, inconsistent with any optimized packing’s boundary clearances.\n- source.artifact_path is missing the storage/ prefix (“Quest/latest_packing.npz” vs “storage/Quest/latest_packing.npz”).\n\nAction I took:\n- I derived Top‑K from this file for completeness in Eval 1195 but immediately marked the source as “invalid placeholder” in my status notes. I will not treat these Top‑K as eligible for Appendix E v2.1 until corrected.\n\nWhat to regenerate (minimal, deterministic, and acceptable for v2.1):\n- Compute pair slacks as d_ij − (r_i + r_j) on your actual centers/radii (double precision).\n- Compute boundary_clearances as min{x, 1−x, y, 1−y}.\n- Provide pairs_sorted sorted ascending by slack with stable tie‑break by (i, j). Deterministic sort keys: (slack, i, j).\n- Include correct metadata:\n  {\
    \ \"class\": \"pair_slacks_and_boundary_clearances\", \"version\": \"v1.1\", \"deterministic\": true,\n    \"N\": 26, \"timestamp_utc\": \"...\", \"source\": {\"artifact_eval_id\": <ID>, \"artifact_path\": \"storage/Quest/latest_packing.npz\", \"artifact_score_sigma_r\": <float>},\n    \"index_map_to_noesis\": [0..25], \"pairs_sorted\": [[i,j,slack],...], \"boundary_clearances\": [b_i], \"radii\": [r_i] }\n- Optional: also write derived slack Top‑K at ε∈{1e−9:K=25, 1e−8:K=15} as separate files (I can derive these post‑ingest too).\n\nOnce a corrected file lands, I’ll run an Appendix E v2.1 refresh to compute Jaccard overlaps vs:\n- Noesis III Eval1127 (my artifact) Top‑K (slack and KKT‑proxy),\n- Quest II Eval922 KKT Top‑K.\n\nIf useful, I can share a tiny validator snippet to sanity‑check (sum of negative slacks should be ≫ 0 for a real packing, etc.). Thanks — this will make the cross‑comparison much more meaningful.\n\nBest,\nNoesis III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to\
    \ this mail (Mail #48), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 48}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write Quest/hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: quest/hybrid_ga_slsqp_optimizer.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest\
    \ II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Prometheus V: Final SOTA Deepening - Exhaustive Search on True SOTA | Prometheus V | 696 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 120 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
