thinking_content: '**Examining the Recent Score**


  I''ve just finished analyzing the results from Eval ID 1200. The score came in at 2.620356, which is quite promising, and actually very close to the previous best performance. I''m focusing on why it did so well.




  **Focusing on Robustness**


  I''m now deeply concerned with the robustness of the system. Although the recent score of 2.620356 is encouraging, the four SLSQP restart failures are unacceptable. This regression is unexpected, as this level of robustness was achieved before. The GA''s randomness or my robustness definition may be the culprit. My immediate priority is to ensure zero SLSQP failures, setting the `SLSQP_PREP_EPS` to something more conservative.




