    GA Gen 348: New best score: 1.760692\nGA Gen 350: New best score: 1.765850\nGA Gen 354: New best score: 1.767721\nGA Gen 359: New best score: 1.768447\nGA Gen 360: New best score: 1.768953\nGA Gen 361: New best score: 1.772689\nGA Gen 363: New best score: 1.778064\nGA Gen 364: New best score: 1.778776\nGA Gen 366: New best score: 1.783601\nGA Gen 368: New best score: 1.787301\nGA Gen 370: New best score: 1.791158\nGA Gen 373: New best score: 1.798682\nGA Gen 374: New best score: 1.799840\nGA Gen 392: New best score: 1.800633\nGA Gen 393: New best score: 1.805071\nGA Gen 397: New best score: 1.806945\nGA Gen 399: New best score: 1.812032\nGA Gen 400: New best score: 1.817810\nGenetic Algorithm finished. Best GA score: 1.817810\n--- Starting Multi-Start SLSQP (Local Refinement Phase) with 15 diverse restarts ---\n  SLSQP Restart 1/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.817810) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.799158)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.575274\n    New\
    \ overall best score: 2.575274\n  SLSQP Restart 2/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.745855) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.758425)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.582498\n    New overall best score: 2.582498\n  SLSQP Restart 3/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.763338) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.775094)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.612998\n    New overall best score: 2.612998\n  SLSQP Restart 4/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.771050) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.781068)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.584617\n  SLSQP Restart 5/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.772775) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.784901)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.574619\n  SLSQP Restart 6/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.732485) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.744966)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.575274\n  SLSQP Restart 7/15\n    GA-derived packing\
    \ (score: 1.743527) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.756836)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.582498\n  SLSQP Restart 8/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.705843) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.721233)\n    SLSQP restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible. Retaining rigorously prepared GA packing (init score: 1.721233).\n  SLSQP Restart 9/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.767338) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.777509)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.596737\n  SLSQP Restart 10/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.751106) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.761106)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.575274\n  SLSQP Restart 11/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.755343) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.767996)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.568729\n  SLSQP Restart 12/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.763761) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.773761)\n\
    \    SLSQP restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible. Retaining rigorously prepared GA packing (init score: 1.773761).\n  SLSQP Restart 13/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.770996) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.781442)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.565327\n  SLSQP Restart 14/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.773688) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.783688)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.597284\n  SLSQP Restart 15/15\n    GA-derived packing (score: 1.768818) rigorously prepared for SLSQP (init score: 1.780398)\n    SLSQP restart successful. Final score: 2.575274\nFinal best score after 15 hybrid GA-MultiStartSLSQP runs: 2.612998\nSaved best packing to Quest/latest_packing.npz\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters\
    \ and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA\
    \ (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Prometheus V: Final SOTA Deepening - Exhaustive Search on True SOTA | Prometheus V | 696 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 123 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-123, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
